WEBVTT

00:40.230 --> 00:44.799
It all starts
with something... magnificent.

00:46.454 --> 00:48.237
A flower.

00:48.238 --> 00:49.457
Just a flower.

00:51.154 --> 00:53.983
Then a honeybee.

00:55.115 --> 00:57.333
Very fragile.

00:57.334 --> 00:59.423
Very complicated.

01:00.729 --> 01:04.601
The bee gathers pollen

01:04.602 --> 01:08.692
and deposits it
in another flower's stigma.

01:08.693 --> 01:11.957
It's like sex but cleaner.

01:11.958 --> 01:13.610
And nobody gets hurt.

01:47.645 --> 01:52.780
A third of our food
is pollinated this way.

01:52.781 --> 01:55.131
You understand
the scope of that?

01:56.176 --> 01:59.352
That's how vital
the bees are, Don.

01:59.353 --> 02:02.051
And they're dying.

02:03.052 --> 02:04.618
Why?

02:04.619 --> 02:07.708
It's like we talked about, cuz.
Remember?

02:07.709 --> 02:11.321
CCD. It's like a pandemic.

02:14.455 --> 02:17.979
Workers desert the queen

02:17.980 --> 02:21.852
until she's all alone
with her young,

02:21.853 --> 02:24.682
and the colony wastes away.

02:28.382 --> 02:31.733
But why do they leave her?

02:32.734 --> 02:34.648
Well...

02:34.649 --> 02:37.651
people claim it's pesticides
or habitat loss.

02:37.652 --> 02:39.914
Or some people think
world governments

02:39.915 --> 02:43.439
and their agro-corporate
overlords

02:43.440 --> 02:47.227
bioengineered CCD
to manipulate food supplies.

02:48.619 --> 02:52.187
But I knew there had to be

02:52.188 --> 02:55.104
a larger organizing
principle at work.

02:56.105 --> 02:57.759
So I studied.

02:58.890 --> 03:00.326
I observed.

03:00.327 --> 03:01.718
Down.

03:01.719 --> 03:03.633
I searched in the ground

03:03.634 --> 03:06.419
and in the stars

03:06.420 --> 03:09.509
until I found it.

03:13.905 --> 03:16.733
It was there all along.

03:20.738 --> 03:23.871
Fucking caging us,
poisoning us,

03:23.872 --> 03:25.917
choking us out.

03:26.875 --> 03:28.397
One. Two.

03:28.398 --> 03:30.834
We are not steering
the ship, Don.

03:30.835 --> 03:32.488
Oh, good job.

03:32.489 --> 03:34.317
They are.

03:37.233 --> 03:40.627
And now it's up to you and me

03:40.628 --> 03:42.630
to stop them.

03:44.849 --> 03:48.069
The training
is for a reason, Don.

03:48.070 --> 03:50.202
It's going to try
and dominate us,

03:50.203 --> 03:53.205
but we're not gonna
let it, are we?

03:53.206 --> 03:56.295
You mean
she'll try to hurt us?

03:56.296 --> 03:58.775
Oh, yes, Don.
It's highly dangerous.

04:03.520 --> 04:05.173
So we have to prepare...

04:05.174 --> 04:08.089
- Down. Up.
- ...our bodies, our brains.

04:08.090 --> 04:10.135
Come on. Come on. Come on.

04:22.191 --> 04:23.800
Why are you laughing?

04:23.801 --> 04:25.541
Sorry, you just look
a little funny doing that,

04:25.542 --> 04:26.890
to be honest. Sorry, Teddy.

04:26.891 --> 04:28.632
- Okay, well, now you do it.
- Okay.

04:33.028 --> 04:34.898
Hey, I think I look funny, too.

04:34.899 --> 04:36.423
Okay.

04:39.034 --> 04:40.556
See? It's good.

04:43.821 --> 04:47.085
Oh, and don't forget
they track it remotely.

04:48.217 --> 04:50.698
And they'll try
and track us, too.

04:52.352 --> 04:56.181
It'll... weevil into your
brainbox every chance it gets,

04:56.182 --> 04:58.836
so we have to fortify
that shit.

05:01.752 --> 05:03.101
Okay.

05:04.494 --> 05:06.321
I'll try.

05:06.322 --> 05:08.497
You-you hear that, though?

05:08.498 --> 05:10.369
Donny?

05:10.370 --> 05:12.633
In your voice, how they
fucked your confidence?

05:14.461 --> 05:16.766
I'm sorry, Teddy.

05:16.767 --> 05:20.293
No. Donny, look at me.

05:21.468 --> 05:22.990
Don't you ever apologize. Ever.

05:22.991 --> 05:25.384
None of this
is your fault. Okay?

05:26.951 --> 05:29.258
Thanks.

05:33.131 --> 05:34.654
It won't play fair.

05:36.396 --> 05:38.528
So we have to be better.

05:41.966 --> 05:44.838
How can you tell them apart?

05:44.839 --> 05:47.754
Well, you have to know
where to look.

05:47.755 --> 05:50.017
There are signs.

05:52.107 --> 05:53.847
What about these people?

05:53.848 --> 05:56.371
No.

05:56.372 --> 05:58.460
No, they're fine.

05:58.461 --> 06:01.463
I mean, they're not fine-fine,

06:01.464 --> 06:03.639
but hollowed.

06:03.640 --> 06:05.206
You know, like the rest of us.

06:05.207 --> 06:06.816
Harmless.

06:06.817 --> 06:09.123
Hopeless.

06:11.605 --> 06:13.867
And that's the way
they planned it.

06:13.868 --> 06:17.697
To make us the same
as the bees.

06:17.698 --> 06:23.093
A dead colony, atomized
in a trillion directions

06:23.094 --> 06:25.749
with no way home again.

06:31.712 --> 06:33.669
-Morning, Ms. Fuller.
-Good morning.

06:33.670 --> 06:35.585
Have a good day.

06:55.562 --> 06:57.606
What does the cream do?

06:57.607 --> 06:58.912
The same.

06:58.913 --> 07:00.653
Mitigation.

07:00.654 --> 07:02.132
Here, get all of it.

07:30.423 --> 07:33.207
What if someone finds out
about what we're doing?

07:33.208 --> 07:34.817
They won't.

07:34.818 --> 07:36.907
No one on earth gives
a single fuck about us.

07:40.998 --> 07:43.784
So until the day comes...

07:45.438 --> 07:48.223
...we clear
the psychic cache, okay?

07:49.224 --> 07:51.312
No distractions.

07:51.313 --> 07:54.316
No gaming, no vape,
no whacking it.

07:56.187 --> 07:59.887
No screens whatsoever,
except for research.

08:01.802 --> 08:03.369
You promise, Don?

08:06.241 --> 08:08.329
I know this is a lot,

08:08.330 --> 08:11.071
but I...
I want you with me on this.

08:11.072 --> 08:13.552
I need you, Don.

08:13.553 --> 08:15.118
- Hmm.
- I know...

08:15.119 --> 08:19.296
you're actually smart and brave,

08:19.297 --> 08:22.126
and no one else sees it but me.

08:24.215 --> 08:28.175
No, you're...
No, you're the smart one.

08:28.176 --> 08:32.049
The brains of this
operation, really. Hmm.

08:33.660 --> 08:38.055
- Hmm. But...
- Is something wrong?

08:39.927 --> 08:41.667
I just...

08:41.668 --> 08:43.320
I don't think I can do this.

08:43.321 --> 08:44.626
Hey.

08:44.627 --> 08:46.106
Come here.

08:46.107 --> 08:47.760
Hmm.

08:47.761 --> 08:49.979
- Give me a hug.
- Ah.

08:49.980 --> 08:51.633
I love you, cuzzie.

08:51.634 --> 08:54.724
I love you, too, man.

08:58.598 --> 09:01.296
You're my best friend
in the whole world.

09:02.253 --> 09:04.298
My only friend.

09:04.299 --> 09:07.302
And I'm doing this
to save you most of all.

09:08.477 --> 09:11.088
I won't let anyone
hurt you, okay?

09:13.177 --> 09:14.351
Okay?

09:14.352 --> 09:16.266
- Okay.
- Never.

09:16.267 --> 09:17.485
Yeah.

09:17.486 --> 09:20.402
Medroxyprogesterone acetate.

09:21.664 --> 09:24.798
It's a progestin-type
hormonal med.

09:26.321 --> 09:28.932
Chemical castration.

09:30.630 --> 09:33.067
- Okay?
- Okay.

09:37.027 --> 09:41.770
In order for us to hit
maximum focus,

09:41.771 --> 09:46.950
we have to clear our heads of
all psychic compulsions, okay?

09:48.517 --> 09:50.170
What does that mean?

09:50.171 --> 09:51.867
Hey, buddy.

09:51.868 --> 09:54.653
Trust me, I've done
a shit ton of research on this.

09:54.654 --> 09:56.655
The more of that
fuck filler we have

09:56.656 --> 09:58.395
jamming up our neurons,

09:58.396 --> 10:01.182
the bigger advantage
it will have over us.

10:02.139 --> 10:03.705
Are you sure?

10:05.012 --> 10:06.492
Yes, Donny, I'm sure.

10:08.581 --> 10:10.844
It's really important, Don.

10:13.934 --> 10:16.022
I just...

10:16.023 --> 10:20.593
wanted to be
with someone someday.

10:22.682 --> 10:24.509
Bud...

10:24.510 --> 10:26.032
you gotta believe me.

10:26.033 --> 10:27.861
I've figured it out.

10:29.602 --> 10:32.952
The part of your brain
that distracts you,

10:32.953 --> 10:34.867
part of your brain
that makes you sad,

10:34.868 --> 10:38.000
it's all connected
to the biological imperative.

10:38.001 --> 10:41.961
These synapses firing off
on procreation

10:41.962 --> 10:46.748
and seed spread and monogamy,

10:46.749 --> 10:49.709
like all these
fucking pain traps.

10:51.275 --> 10:55.322
It's all...
it's all neurons, dude.

10:55.323 --> 10:57.847
You just have to harness them.

10:59.327 --> 11:02.068
Once you kill the urges,
like I have,

11:02.069 --> 11:05.159
you'll be your own master.

11:07.117 --> 11:09.075
No one can fuck with you.

11:09.076 --> 11:11.469
You'll be totally free.

11:12.775 --> 11:14.908
Don't you want to be free?

11:17.084 --> 11:18.780
Yes.

11:18.781 --> 11:20.566
So you ready?

11:22.742 --> 11:25.483
Let's do this.

11:26.615 --> 11:28.224
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

11:28.225 --> 11:30.183
Okay, so, uh...

11:30.184 --> 11:32.359
Lean over the chair
and talk to me.

11:32.360 --> 11:34.230
- It'll distract you.
- Yeah.

11:34.231 --> 11:36.406
How are you, Teddy?

11:36.407 --> 11:37.930
I'm doing great, man.

11:37.931 --> 11:39.584
How are you?

11:39.585 --> 11:42.282
Uh, I'm doing good.

11:42.283 --> 11:44.763
So, you excited to be free?

11:44.764 --> 11:46.199
Yeah.

11:46.200 --> 11:48.331
What does free
feel like to you?

11:48.332 --> 11:50.682
I guess it...

11:50.683 --> 11:53.293
feels like when we were little,

11:53.294 --> 11:55.687
before things got bad.

11:55.688 --> 11:58.604
When everyone was still here.

11:59.779 --> 12:02.955
Hey, hey.

12:02.956 --> 12:06.001
I know it's been hard, man.

12:06.002 --> 12:10.441
But we're gonna get it
back again. I promise.

12:11.442 --> 12:14.053
All we've lost,

12:14.054 --> 12:17.187
all these years, all the shit
that's been done to us...

12:18.493 --> 12:21.365
...we're setting that shit
right again.

12:22.540 --> 12:25.238
And no one can fuck with us.

12:25.239 --> 12:27.240
Not even ourselves.

12:27.241 --> 12:29.983
- Morning, Corey.
- Good morning, Michelle.

12:56.966 --> 12:58.706
I believe every company
should strive

12:58.707 --> 13:00.882
to form a diverse table.

13:00.883 --> 13:03.276
If the people on your team
are from diverse backgrounds,

13:03.277 --> 13:05.800
they'll find new and creative
solutions to problems

13:05.801 --> 13:07.541
rather than just iterating.

13:07.542 --> 13:09.195
We need to find
the next generation

13:09.196 --> 13:10.544
of diverse engineers,

13:10.545 --> 13:12.938
diverse biologists,
diverse doctors.

13:12.939 --> 13:15.244
Because it's not just
diverse employees,

13:15.245 --> 13:16.768
it's diverse thinking.

13:16.769 --> 13:19.509
It's about using
our corporate resources

13:19.510 --> 13:24.253
to empower people of different
skills and identities...

13:24.254 --> 13:25.820
Holy fucking fucker.

13:25.821 --> 13:27.039
Jesus Christ.

13:27.040 --> 13:28.954
Every time. What is it?

13:28.955 --> 13:30.651
"Skills and identities
to foster..."

13:30.652 --> 13:31.826
To foster a new
generation of Auxolith talent.

13:31.827 --> 13:33.002
Okay, let's reset.

13:34.134 --> 13:35.700
It's too many "diverses," Chris.

13:35.701 --> 13:37.266
It's-- I'm going,
"diverse, diverse, diverse."

13:37.267 --> 13:38.877
Like "Buh-duh,
buh-duh, buh-duh."

13:38.878 --> 13:40.530
Like a fucking metronome.

13:40.531 --> 13:43.795
Well, uh, [clears throat],
it is diversity training.

13:43.796 --> 13:45.448
Yeah, but it's too many, Chris.

13:45.449 --> 13:47.712
Can we try to diversify
the language a little bit?

13:47.713 --> 13:50.018
No, sure.

13:50.019 --> 13:51.760
Let's go again.

13:56.460 --> 13:57.939
Okay, so that's it then.

13:57.940 --> 13:59.854
You just have
the investor call with Sara

13:59.855 --> 14:03.510
and a VC with Wieden+Kennedy
at 9:00 that you can do remote.

14:03.511 --> 14:06.382
Thank you, Corey.

14:06.383 --> 14:07.819
The 5:30 thing.

14:07.820 --> 14:09.342
Uh-huh?

14:09.343 --> 14:10.691
Look, I know you sent
the email already,

14:10.692 --> 14:12.040
but I need you
to let everyone know

14:12.041 --> 14:13.433
that they are free
to leave at 5:30

14:13.434 --> 14:15.478
from now on,
starting today, okay?

14:15.479 --> 14:17.437
But do it in a way
that's, you know,

14:17.438 --> 14:18.960
what we talked about.

14:18.961 --> 14:20.701
- Yeah, of course.
- We need to send the message

14:20.702 --> 14:22.398
that we have a new culture
here now.

14:22.399 --> 14:24.139
Where people should,
yes, of course,

14:24.140 --> 14:26.228
feel free to leave at 5:30
and be with their families.

14:26.229 --> 14:28.143
No one is gonna be overworked
like in the past.

14:28.144 --> 14:30.232
No more unpleasant incidents.

14:30.233 --> 14:32.321
But, of course,
it's not compulsory.

14:32.322 --> 14:34.236
And, obviously, if people
still have work to do,

14:34.237 --> 14:36.282
they should absolutely stay
and continue to work.

14:36.283 --> 14:38.632
- Yeah.
- But it's not strictly enforced.

14:38.633 --> 14:40.852
Although we still do want
to meet quotas.

14:40.853 --> 14:42.984
So if we can do that
with no pressure,

14:42.985 --> 14:44.943
just remembering, you know,
we are running a business here,

14:44.944 --> 14:47.075
so "let your conscience
guide you" kind of thing.

14:47.076 --> 14:48.511
Yeah? Good?

14:48.512 --> 14:49.904
I'll definitely let them know.

14:49.905 --> 14:51.645
Great.

14:51.646 --> 14:53.038
New era.

14:53.039 --> 14:55.476
Thank you, Corey.

15:02.352 --> 15:03.657
Thanks, Tony.

15:03.658 --> 15:05.615
Feel free to leave early.

15:05.616 --> 15:07.443
I mean, unless you're busy.

15:07.444 --> 15:10.490
Or you have things to do,
but feel free if you can.

15:10.491 --> 15:12.144
- Up to you.
- Yes, ma'am.

15:12.145 --> 15:13.928
Your call.

15:15.365 --> 15:16.931
♪ I told you so ♪

15:16.932 --> 15:21.457
♪ You know I hate to say,
but I told you so ♪

15:21.458 --> 15:25.374
♪ You can kiss
a hundred boys in bars ♪

15:25.375 --> 15:28.073
♪ Shoot another shot,
try to stop the feeling ♪

15:28.074 --> 15:29.683
♪ Well, I told you so ♪

15:29.684 --> 15:33.469
♪ You can say
it's just the way you are ♪

15:33.470 --> 15:37.299
♪ Make a new excuse,
nother stupid reason ♪

15:37.300 --> 15:39.214
- ♪ Good luck, babe ♪
- ♪ Well, good luck ♪

15:39.215 --> 15:41.608
- ♪ Well, good luck, babe ♪
- ♪ Well, good luck ♪

15:41.609 --> 15:42.957
♪ You'd have to stop... ♪

15:47.658 --> 15:49.703
- ♪ Well, good luck, babe ♪
- ♪ Well, good luck ♪

15:49.704 --> 15:53.838
♪ You'd have to stop the world
just to stop the feeling... ♪

15:55.405 --> 15:57.494
Come on, come on.

16:16.035 --> 16:17.078
No.

16:26.610 --> 16:28.394
Shit! Fuck, fuck!

17:29.630 --> 17:31.675
No, no, no! Stay back with her.

17:41.424 --> 17:43.470
Spray! Spray!

18:06.319 --> 18:07.797
Really have to hurry, bud.

18:07.798 --> 18:10.539
- Um, I know. I'm sorry.
- Okay, quick as you can.

18:10.540 --> 18:12.802
It's like GPS, remember?

18:12.803 --> 18:15.327
If its hair is still attached,
it can track us remotely,

18:15.328 --> 18:17.111
so we want to go
as quick as we can.

18:17.112 --> 18:19.026
Okay.

18:19.027 --> 18:20.375
Is it working?

18:20.376 --> 18:23.465
Not much is coming off.

18:23.466 --> 18:25.424
Y-You really, you really
got to run it through. Harder.

18:25.425 --> 18:27.252
But wh-what if I cut her?

18:27.253 --> 18:29.558
Don! Do it harder!
You won't cut her!

18:29.559 --> 18:30.646
Okay.

18:54.019 --> 18:56.194
Man, I feel good. Don't you?

18:56.195 --> 18:57.499
I guess.

18:57.500 --> 18:59.414
You were amazing, cuz.

18:59.415 --> 19:00.633
I was?

19:00.634 --> 19:02.243
Oh, yeah.

19:02.244 --> 19:04.724
Fucking alpha king shit.

19:04.725 --> 19:07.596
Well, thanks, man.

19:07.597 --> 19:09.033
I knew you could do it.

19:09.034 --> 19:12.515
Sure enough,
you fucking crushed it.

19:18.782 --> 19:20.479
Incredible.

19:20.480 --> 19:22.263
What is?

19:22.264 --> 19:24.918
Just the detail.

19:24.919 --> 19:26.572
The best I've seen.

19:26.573 --> 19:29.705
Uh, how can you tell
she's an alien?

19:29.706 --> 19:34.058
Well, the signs are obvious.

19:34.059 --> 19:36.277
They did a hell of a job on it,
but the tells are there.

19:36.278 --> 19:38.497
Narrow feet.

19:38.498 --> 19:41.456
Thin cuticles.

19:41.457 --> 19:44.069
Slight overbite.

19:47.333 --> 19:50.161
Semi-obtruding earlobes.

19:50.162 --> 19:51.423
See?

19:51.424 --> 19:53.947
High hair density.

19:53.948 --> 19:57.951
You won't notice unless you know
what you're looking for.

19:57.952 --> 20:00.301
Guess I can see it.

20:00.302 --> 20:04.871
It's like,
if you don't cook steaks a lot,

20:04.872 --> 20:06.742
you won't know
when it's cooked medium-rare,

20:06.743 --> 20:11.269
but if you cook steaks
all the time, you just know.

20:11.270 --> 20:13.053
You don't even
have to cut into it.

20:13.054 --> 20:15.622
You just... know.

20:18.364 --> 20:20.974
Hey, hey, um...

20:20.975 --> 20:23.237
Why are we doing this?

20:23.238 --> 20:24.804
Is she itchy?

20:24.805 --> 20:27.676
No, Don. It's not itchy.

20:27.677 --> 20:31.071
Its genetic structure
is the same as ours,

20:31.072 --> 20:34.074
uh, but its nervous system
is different.

20:34.075 --> 20:36.729
The antihistamine reacts
to the neurotransmitters

20:36.730 --> 20:39.819
in its nervous system
and weakens it.

20:39.820 --> 20:43.127
We're just leveling
the playing field.

20:43.128 --> 20:46.608
It's not torture.
Torture is what it's done to us.

20:46.609 --> 20:49.089
Huh.

20:49.090 --> 20:51.178
The sedative
should wear off soon.

20:51.179 --> 20:52.788
Should we go get dressed?

20:52.789 --> 20:54.660
-Okay.
-Okay, come on.

21:08.936 --> 21:11.373
- Is it too tight?
- No, man.

21:12.896 --> 21:15.028
No, this was my dad's shit.

21:15.029 --> 21:17.726
He left it behind for a reason,

21:17.727 --> 21:19.773
so that it could be
put to good use.

21:20.817 --> 21:23.080
Everything's for a reason, Don.

21:24.299 --> 21:26.082
It's too tight.

21:26.083 --> 21:28.433
- I look stupid.
- No, you don't.

21:28.434 --> 21:31.175
You look fine, honestly.
You look fine.

21:31.176 --> 21:33.786
Anyway...
what's that swine gonna do,

21:33.787 --> 21:36.702
call the fashion police
and arrest you?

21:36.703 --> 21:39.357
This isn't about her.

21:39.358 --> 21:41.141
Hey.

21:41.142 --> 21:44.318
It is not in control anymore.

21:44.319 --> 21:45.625
We are.

21:47.235 --> 21:50.672
Besides, I'll be doing
most of the talking anyway.

21:50.673 --> 21:53.980
In fact, maybe don't say much.

21:53.981 --> 21:55.895
Like, you-you don't really
have to say much.

21:55.896 --> 21:57.766
Okay.

21:57.767 --> 22:00.856
Like, don't talk at all, maybe.

22:00.857 --> 22:02.380
Oh.

22:26.753 --> 22:28.189
Welcome.

22:30.060 --> 22:32.148
Are you conscious?

22:32.149 --> 22:35.195
- What?
- Is she conscious?

22:35.196 --> 22:38.720
I can only proceed if
you're fully conscious, so...

22:38.721 --> 22:40.505
Uh...

22:40.506 --> 22:41.854
What?

22:41.855 --> 22:43.856
Yes. Greetings.

22:43.857 --> 22:45.380
This is my home.

22:46.947 --> 22:48.470
Where...

22:51.865 --> 22:54.562
This i-- this is a hospital?

22:54.563 --> 22:58.523
- No, this is not a hospital.
- Is this a...

22:58.524 --> 23:01.526
Fuck it. I'm just gonna start.

23:01.527 --> 23:04.659
"Welcome to the headquarters
of the human resistance.

23:04.660 --> 23:07.314
"Despite our general suspicion
and disavowal

23:07.315 --> 23:09.360
"of all extant governing bodies,

23:09.361 --> 23:11.927
"and despite the fact that you,
as an Andromedan,

23:11.928 --> 23:13.973
"are not subject to
the human rights guidelines

23:13.974 --> 23:16.018
"detailed in
the Geneva Conventions,

23:16.019 --> 23:17.890
"we nevertheless endeavor
to adhere to those guidelines

23:17.891 --> 23:20.589
out of the humanist principles
to which they aspire."

23:21.808 --> 23:23.330
What is happening?

23:23.331 --> 23:25.289
I'm explaining to you
that I would like to keep

23:25.290 --> 23:30.250
all of this very aboveboard
and civilized, so...

23:30.251 --> 23:31.860
Where's my hair?

23:31.861 --> 23:34.776
- Your hair's been destroyed.
- You shaved off my hair?

23:34.777 --> 23:36.865
Yes, we've shaved off your hair.

23:36.866 --> 23:39.346
Why have you shaved off my hair?

23:39.347 --> 23:42.481
To prevent you
from contacting your ship.

23:43.525 --> 23:45.745
- My ship?
- Your ship.

23:46.702 --> 23:48.704
What ship?

23:49.749 --> 23:51.228
Your mother ship.

23:53.187 --> 23:56.102
- Okay.
- Full disclosure:

23:56.103 --> 23:57.495
I've also applied a thin layer

23:57.496 --> 23:59.279
of antihistamine cream
to your skin...

23:59.280 --> 24:01.368
- Excuse me. Listen to me.
- ...which we'll need to reapply

24:01.369 --> 24:02.543
every day
for full effectiveness.

24:02.544 --> 24:04.329
Listen to me.

24:06.243 --> 24:08.027
I'm listening.

24:08.028 --> 24:09.203
Right.

24:10.813 --> 24:13.641
H-Here's what's gonna happen.

24:13.642 --> 24:17.079
And I want to be clear,
I'm not threatening you.

24:17.080 --> 24:18.385
Or you.

24:18.386 --> 24:21.475
But the following is
my best guess

24:21.476 --> 24:25.436
of how the next 48 hours
are likely to transpire.

24:25.437 --> 24:27.568
The police
and soon thereafter the FBI

24:27.569 --> 24:29.004
will begin a statewide manhunt

24:29.005 --> 24:31.267
using all of the methods
at their disposal

24:31.268 --> 24:34.967
and the combined resources
of neighboring jurisdictions.

24:34.968 --> 24:38.579
My company is a key job creator

24:38.580 --> 24:40.668
and economic engine
of the region.

24:40.669 --> 24:42.148
I am crucial.

24:42.149 --> 24:45.151
Think of it like
you've abducted the governor

24:45.152 --> 24:46.631
but worse.

24:46.632 --> 24:48.197
That's the level
of bureaucratic urgency

24:48.198 --> 24:49.416
you're contending with here.

24:49.417 --> 24:51.418
In all humility, I can say that.

24:51.419 --> 24:54.639
I'm also a high-profile
female corporate executive.

24:54.640 --> 24:56.075
Does that add a certain,

24:56.076 --> 24:57.598
you know,
politicized optics to this?

24:57.599 --> 24:58.991
I would say absolutely.

24:58.992 --> 25:01.210
I would say
that's a tremendous factor

25:01.211 --> 25:03.256
for you to consider here.

25:03.257 --> 25:05.345
Now, I don't make the rules,
and I don't enforce anything,

25:05.346 --> 25:08.870
and I am not in charge
of the situation in this room.

25:08.871 --> 25:10.655
You are.

25:10.656 --> 25:13.875
But you are not in charge
of what is happening out there,

25:13.876 --> 25:17.183
and what is happening out there
is a rapid cross-coordination

25:17.184 --> 25:19.228
of law enforcement
and digital media,

25:19.229 --> 25:20.621
which is all leading
quite inevitably

25:20.622 --> 25:22.580
to your imprisonment.

25:22.581 --> 25:25.060
And very likely worse.

25:25.061 --> 25:26.802
If I can be frank.

25:28.630 --> 25:30.892
I-I'm not privy to
what their methods might be

25:30.893 --> 25:34.418
under extreme duress,
or yours for that matter,

25:34.419 --> 25:38.247
but I can assure you that
there is no possible scenario

25:38.248 --> 25:39.858
where you benefit
from this incident,

25:39.859 --> 25:43.122
unless you cooperate with me
right now

25:43.123 --> 25:46.431
and negotiate a deal that's fair
and advantageous to us both.

25:54.090 --> 25:55.221
Okay.

25:57.442 --> 25:59.139
Wow.

26:00.662 --> 26:03.665
That was really good.
That was really good.

26:05.232 --> 26:07.102
My pulse is racing right now.

26:07.103 --> 26:09.235
Um...

26:09.236 --> 26:10.758
Fuck.

26:10.759 --> 26:13.326
You got a real human response
out of me there,

26:13.327 --> 26:16.721
which is impressive given your
cellular composition and all.

26:16.722 --> 26:19.071
- It-It's the truth.
- Well, no, it's not the truth.

26:19.072 --> 26:20.942
Nothing you say is true.

26:20.943 --> 26:25.078
Objective human truth has no
value in Andromedan cognition.

26:26.209 --> 26:28.689
L-Let's just unpack
the problem here.

26:28.690 --> 26:30.778
"Unpack"? Wow, heady shit.

26:30.779 --> 26:33.999
Sure, let's unpack
the old fact bag, shall we?

26:34.000 --> 26:39.570
You are a high-ranking official
in the royal Andromedan court,

26:39.571 --> 26:43.748
and you've aided your species
in the techno-enslavement

26:43.749 --> 26:45.706
and the agro-corporate
disintegration

26:45.707 --> 26:48.317
of planet Earth, okay?

26:48.318 --> 26:50.755
And we need you to bring us
to your mother ship

26:50.756 --> 26:53.148
on the night
of the lunar eclipse

26:53.149 --> 26:56.325
to broker a sit-down
with your royal superiors.

26:56.326 --> 26:59.067
How's that?
Fucking unpacked enough for ya?

26:59.068 --> 27:00.634
I hear where you're coming from.

27:00.635 --> 27:02.201
I do.

27:02.202 --> 27:04.464
And I respectfully disagree.

27:04.465 --> 27:06.380
On which part?

27:07.816 --> 27:09.817
- Primarily, I'm not an alien.
- You are.

27:09.818 --> 27:12.516
I've done thermal imaging
on your face.

27:12.517 --> 27:14.953
There's Andromedan code
all over your Instagram.

27:14.954 --> 27:17.043
You're barely even hiding it.

27:18.392 --> 27:20.088
I mean, look at you.

27:20.089 --> 27:24.136
I'm supposed to believe
you're a 45-year-old woman?

27:24.137 --> 27:25.659
Human woman?

27:25.660 --> 27:27.531
I mean, I follow a very strict

27:27.532 --> 27:30.403
reverse-aging diet
and therapy program.

27:30.404 --> 27:32.927
It's very expensive, as you can
imagine, but I'm not an alien.

27:34.321 --> 27:36.061
Well, there's really
no time for this.

27:36.062 --> 27:37.845
- You are.
- I'm not.

27:43.765 --> 27:45.418
All right, then.

27:45.419 --> 27:47.986
We're going to give you
the night...

27:47.987 --> 27:50.249
to give your statement.

27:50.250 --> 27:51.990
My statement?

27:51.991 --> 27:53.644
That you will give
to your emperor...

27:53.645 --> 27:54.993
Uh-huh.

27:54.994 --> 27:57.299
...to grant us passage
to your ship

27:57.300 --> 28:00.346
and negotiate your species'
withdrawal from planet Earth.

28:00.347 --> 28:03.175
Right. C-Could we have
a dialogue about this, please?

28:03.176 --> 28:06.700
Because what you're asking me
to do is not quite clear to me.

28:06.701 --> 28:08.136
I think it is.

28:08.137 --> 28:10.923
And I want you to know...

28:13.012 --> 28:15.492
...this is really difficult
for me as well.

28:16.624 --> 28:18.103
You killed my family.

28:18.104 --> 28:21.497
You killed my community.
You killed my coworkers.

28:21.498 --> 28:23.499
You killed the bees.

28:23.500 --> 28:25.414
So, given that,

28:25.415 --> 28:28.896
you should really appreciate
how super professional

28:28.897 --> 28:31.204
I'm being right now
by not gutting you.

28:42.737 --> 28:46.610
So, your sustenance
and waste disposal

28:46.611 --> 28:48.437
will be attended to
in the morning.

28:48.438 --> 28:51.353
Uh, I haven't gathered
adequate data

28:51.354 --> 28:54.400
on what type of sleep
you require, if any,

28:54.401 --> 28:56.838
but you should try
and get some, okay?

29:00.450 --> 29:02.277
I'm very sorry.

29:02.278 --> 29:06.630
I think that we maybe
got off on the wrong foot.

29:06.631 --> 29:10.547
And I would love to keep
the conversation going, please.

29:11.461 --> 29:14.550
Excuse me, please?

29:14.551 --> 29:16.465
Don. Don. Don, come on.

29:16.466 --> 29:18.555
Come on, let's keep talking.

29:19.513 --> 29:20.993
Please?

29:23.430 --> 29:24.648
Please?!

29:39.272 --> 29:40.968
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

29:43.015 --> 29:45.756
Don, Don, Don, Don!

30:14.873 --> 30:16.961
Hey.

30:16.962 --> 30:23.141
We can't see it as
a human woman, you know?

30:23.142 --> 30:26.231
It's not a person
named Michelle Fuller.

30:26.232 --> 30:29.104
It's the Fuller Humanoid.
That's all it is.

30:30.279 --> 30:33.238
Even if it was human--
and it's not--

30:33.239 --> 30:34.892
it's still evil.

30:34.893 --> 30:38.112
Pure corporate evil.

30:38.113 --> 30:41.246
It's killing our planet, cuzzie.

30:41.247 --> 30:42.856
It was the lead executive

30:42.857 --> 30:44.597
on the neonicotinoid
linked to honeybee death.

30:44.598 --> 30:46.556
It only knows cruelty.

30:49.255 --> 30:51.474
Is it an alien?

30:52.780 --> 30:54.564
Yes.

30:59.744 --> 31:01.833
It knows you're watching
right now, too.

31:02.921 --> 31:04.530
It's trying to gain
your sympathy.

31:04.531 --> 31:06.140
That shitty way
that you feel right now,

31:06.141 --> 31:07.794
that's how it wants you to feel.

31:07.795 --> 31:11.058
It's mastered the art
of emotional manipulation.

31:11.059 --> 31:12.581
I'm sorry.

31:12.582 --> 31:17.456
I-I promise
I won't mess this up, Teddy.

31:17.457 --> 31:19.633
Don't apologize, remember?

31:20.808 --> 31:23.592
We just stick to the plan.

31:23.593 --> 31:26.291
We have four days
until the lunar eclipse,

31:26.292 --> 31:29.816
when the Andromedan ship
can return undetected. Yeah?

31:29.817 --> 31:31.644
Yeah.

31:31.645 --> 31:36.475
So, we need the Fuller Humanoid
to help us make contact

31:36.476 --> 31:40.653
so we can fight
for our self-worth.

31:40.654 --> 31:43.656
For our material existence, Don.

31:43.657 --> 31:46.877
You know, I... wish
I could fix everything

31:46.878 --> 31:49.750
that's been done to you.

31:50.707 --> 31:52.752
This is not about me, Don.

31:54.886 --> 31:57.365
This is about everyone.

31:57.366 --> 32:01.718
And one day very soon,
you'll see.

32:03.633 --> 32:07.549
And the world will see you
as you truly are.

32:07.550 --> 32:09.247
A hero.

32:09.248 --> 32:13.425
That's why we stick to...

32:13.426 --> 32:17.168
We stick to...

32:17.169 --> 32:19.432
- the plan.
- Plan.

32:20.825 --> 32:23.130
- Uh...
- See? You're listening.

32:23.131 --> 32:25.090
Uh, yeah.

32:59.298 --> 33:02.126
I don't even
fucking know what's in it.

33:02.127 --> 33:04.998
I just eat the poison
they give me.

33:04.999 --> 33:07.783
But I know...

33:07.784 --> 33:10.438
they hide shit in there,

33:10.439 --> 33:13.965
to program my cells...

33:15.227 --> 33:17.881
...my blood.

33:17.882 --> 33:21.319
I see what their plan is, okay?

33:21.320 --> 33:23.756
They sell me the sickness,
then they sell me the cure,

33:23.757 --> 33:26.715
and it's money on both sides

33:26.716 --> 33:29.066
from the mind control,

33:29.067 --> 33:33.461
um... industry, okay?

33:33.462 --> 33:35.464
Get it?

33:36.465 --> 33:38.554
But I'll do it for you.

33:39.991 --> 33:42.080
You know, if it helps.

33:43.559 --> 33:45.300
If it makes me not like me.

33:46.301 --> 33:47.432
Like I am, you know?

33:47.433 --> 33:50.391
Like, weak.

33:50.392 --> 33:54.396
Your slob, cunt mom
will do it for you, baby.

33:55.484 --> 33:58.399
Just don't let them
get you, too.

34:35.872 --> 34:37.221
You can go faster.

34:37.222 --> 34:39.137
- This isn't the spa.
- Okay. Okay.

34:49.930 --> 34:51.844
PODCAST HOST [over headphones]:
With scientific evidence

34:51.845 --> 34:53.889
pointing to the potential
of other life

34:53.890 --> 34:57.893
even on our own planet
that we can't comprehend yet,

34:57.894 --> 35:00.244
and with unexplainable
phenomenon

35:00.245 --> 35:02.986
experienced by people daily
in the skies,

35:02.987 --> 35:06.250
in the oceans, and even
in their own backyard,

35:06.251 --> 35:08.643
I think it's kind of
just a little uninformed

35:08.644 --> 35:11.385
to not at least acknowledge
the potential

35:11.386 --> 35:15.607
that humankind may not be
the only intelligent life

35:15.608 --> 35:18.218
to ever exist
throughout the galaxy.

35:34.192 --> 35:35.409
...other higher-intelligent

35:35.410 --> 35:36.932
beings somewhere.

35:36.933 --> 35:38.891
I don't know if they're
coming, like I said,

35:38.892 --> 35:40.849
through the vibrations,
coming through frequencies

35:40.850 --> 35:42.547
into our world,
or if they're coming through...

35:42.548 --> 35:44.418
...trillions and billions

35:44.419 --> 35:46.942
of miles of space,
which seems kind of ridiculous

35:46.943 --> 35:48.553
when you think about it, but...

35:48.554 --> 35:50.859
- There's a whole...
-But what if it's...

35:50.860 --> 35:52.513
what if it's both
of those things?

35:52.514 --> 35:54.254
What if it's not one
or the other?

35:54.255 --> 35:56.344
It-it could be a
mixture of everything. -Yeah.

36:00.740 --> 36:02.523
Hey.

36:02.524 --> 36:04.612
Saw you there. You all right?

36:04.613 --> 36:07.876
Uh, yeah. I'm fine.

36:07.877 --> 36:10.314
- How are you?
-  I'm good.

36:10.315 --> 36:13.056
Off to work, then, or...?

36:13.057 --> 36:15.188
Uh-huh.

36:15.189 --> 36:16.755
I-I'm sorry, man.

36:16.756 --> 36:18.322
I know you're like,
"This fucking guy," right?

36:18.323 --> 36:19.453
No, no.

36:19.454 --> 36:21.107
No, it's all right. It's just...

36:21.108 --> 36:24.067
You know, we haven't had
a chance to catch up in a while,

36:24.068 --> 36:26.069
'cause, you know...

36:26.070 --> 36:28.854
all the shit, and, uh, yeah.

36:28.855 --> 36:31.074
Just wanted to check up on you.

36:31.075 --> 36:33.032
Casey, I'm good. What's up?

36:33.033 --> 36:35.208
Nothing's up, man. I just...

36:35.209 --> 36:36.818
I know I wasn't always
the best babysitter

36:36.819 --> 36:38.820
back in the day, but, um...

36:38.821 --> 36:41.128
I do want you to be okay.

36:43.696 --> 36:46.567
You still up there with Don?

36:46.568 --> 36:47.742
Yep.

36:47.743 --> 36:49.962
Great. Well, uh...

36:49.963 --> 36:51.442
I think about you sometimes.

36:51.443 --> 36:54.315
Not... not in a weird way,
just... Yeah.

36:55.664 --> 36:57.274
I'm a different guy now--
I've grown up--

36:57.275 --> 37:00.016
so if you ever need help
with anything, just...

37:01.017 --> 37:03.149
I'm good.

37:03.150 --> 37:05.282
I just gotta get to work, so...

37:05.283 --> 37:06.805
Maybe I'll stop by sometime.

37:06.806 --> 37:10.940
Yeah, I mean, I-I'm j...
I'm super busy right now.

37:11.985 --> 37:13.290
- Crazy busy.
- Right.

37:13.291 --> 37:16.119
But, um,
yeah, maybe sometime later.

37:16.120 --> 37:18.904
Later, yeah. All right.

37:18.905 --> 37:20.559
Cool. See ya.

37:21.560 --> 37:23.517
Take it easy.

37:23.518 --> 37:24.998
See ya, Teddy.

37:26.695 --> 37:28.696
HOST 2 [over headphones]: Some
people say they're all demons.

37:28.697 --> 37:31.830
A lot of people think they're
higher-intelligent beings

37:31.831 --> 37:35.399
from a different wavelength.

37:35.400 --> 37:36.748
That's a possibility,
too, I guess.

37:36.749 --> 37:38.271
I-I don't know anything.

37:38.272 --> 37:40.230
So I'm not saying, like,
one way or the other.

37:40.231 --> 37:42.275
I just, personally,
I have my opinion,

37:42.276 --> 37:44.234
and I think it's somehow
all connected.

37:44.235 --> 37:45.974
HOST 1 [over headphones]:
I think that

37:45.975 --> 37:49.413
all of those things
are each a small part of...

37:49.414 --> 37:50.762
How you doing?

37:50.763 --> 37:52.633
- What's up, man?
-Morning.

37:52.634 --> 37:54.766
HOST 2 [over headphones]:
I honestly start to believe

37:54.767 --> 37:56.681
that we're all in,
like, a simulation.

37:56.682 --> 37:58.204
And I don't want to say
it's like The Matrix, but...

38:04.037 --> 38:05.429
What's wrong, Tina?

38:05.430 --> 38:08.432
My frickin' hand
is still killing me.

38:08.433 --> 38:11.391
Christ. Did you file that shit
with OSHA yet?

38:11.392 --> 38:14.960
I looked into it, but I...

38:14.961 --> 38:17.789
I don't think it's a violation.

38:17.790 --> 38:21.140
Tina, their machinery cut you,

38:21.141 --> 38:23.273
and you get punished
for missing quotas?

38:23.274 --> 38:25.971
That's a... that's a violation.

38:25.972 --> 38:27.582
Fucking demons.

38:29.454 --> 38:31.673
I just don't want any trouble.

38:36.069 --> 38:37.461
Don't you worry.

38:37.462 --> 38:39.724
One day soon,
it's all gonna change.

38:39.725 --> 38:42.336
They're not gonna get away
with this shit in the end, okay?

38:43.424 --> 38:45.033
I promise you that.

38:45.034 --> 38:46.687
On Monday afternoon,

38:46.688 --> 38:49.473
following what coworkers
describe as a routine workday,

38:49.474 --> 38:53.172
Auxolith Biomedical CEO
Michelle Fuller

38:53.173 --> 38:55.783
got into her car,
passed the security gate

38:55.784 --> 38:58.656
at Auxolith headquarters
in Fayette County, Georgia,

38:58.657 --> 39:00.527
and drove towards home.

39:00.528 --> 39:02.790
That was nearly 48 hours ago.

39:02.791 --> 39:05.053
No one has heard from her since.

39:05.054 --> 39:07.404
Authorities now believe
there is a strong chance...

39:07.405 --> 39:08.796
Hey.

39:08.797 --> 39:10.189
Oh, yo. What up, Carlos?

39:10.190 --> 39:12.365
I brought some
fresh honey in for toast.

39:12.366 --> 39:13.627
Oh, great.

39:13.628 --> 39:15.325
- Thank you, Teddy.
- Yeah.

39:15.326 --> 39:16.978
A furious statewide
manhunt is now underway,

39:16.979 --> 39:19.590
with state police urging
Fayette County locals

39:19.591 --> 39:23.071
to come forward with
any information at all.

39:23.072 --> 39:25.073
Given Fuller's wealth
and high profile,

39:25.074 --> 39:27.511
state police are not ruling out
the possibility

39:27.512 --> 39:30.078
that Fuller is being held
for ransom,

39:30.079 --> 39:32.646
though, as of yet,
there is no evidence

39:32.647 --> 39:34.431
to suggest this might be
the case.

39:34.432 --> 39:36.259
The only clue authorities...

40:12.121 --> 40:14.209
Hey, cuz. Did she eat?

40:14.210 --> 40:15.602
No.

40:15.603 --> 40:17.038
Bedpan?

40:17.039 --> 40:18.389
No.

40:22.175 --> 40:25.569
Maybe she's too scared to go?

40:25.570 --> 40:27.571
No, she's not too scared to go.

40:27.572 --> 40:30.748
It's trying to pity-trap
our asses.

40:30.749 --> 40:32.663
It's a ploy.

40:32.664 --> 40:34.752
We're not gonna let it
pity-trap us, are we?

40:37.103 --> 40:38.408
No.

40:38.409 --> 40:39.844
Just stay over there.

40:39.845 --> 40:41.586
Okay, Teddy.

41:02.258 --> 41:05.783
MICHELLE [over recorder]: Um,
I am an alien from outer space.

41:05.784 --> 41:10.527
I live here on planet Earth,
but I am not a human being.

41:10.528 --> 41:13.747
My mother ship
is coming to Earth,

41:13.748 --> 41:16.620
and I would like to bring
my new friend with me.

41:16.621 --> 41:17.970
Thanks.

41:20.059 --> 41:21.451
Uh-huh.

41:21.452 --> 41:23.888
So...

41:23.889 --> 41:26.151
this is a joke, then?

41:26.152 --> 41:30.155
You're trying to simulate
sapient humor, or...

41:30.156 --> 41:32.244
That was the best I could do.

41:32.245 --> 41:33.724
This is the best you could do?

41:33.725 --> 41:35.509
You didn't even say it
in your own language.

41:36.989 --> 41:39.077
Sorry, that was the best
I could do.

41:39.078 --> 41:41.385
No, it isn't.

41:42.777 --> 41:45.649
What would you like me
to say, then?

41:45.650 --> 41:47.302
Well, I already did that.

41:47.303 --> 41:51.089
Um, I would like you
to request an audience

41:51.090 --> 41:54.048
with your emperor
to discuss the terms

41:54.049 --> 41:56.224
of your species' withdrawal
from Earth.

41:56.225 --> 41:57.443
And I did that.

41:57.444 --> 41:58.792
But convincingly.

41:58.793 --> 42:00.403
Well, that's gonna be difficult.

42:00.404 --> 42:01.753
Why?

42:03.058 --> 42:06.758
At the risk of repeating myself,
I'm not an alien.

42:13.852 --> 42:15.940
Teddy?

42:15.941 --> 42:17.594
What?

42:17.595 --> 42:21.641
I thought all night
about our situation here,

42:21.642 --> 42:23.730
and I think I know
what's going on.

42:23.731 --> 42:26.167
Okay. Yeah, please,
enlighten me.

42:26.168 --> 42:28.779
So, look, I feel qualified here

42:28.780 --> 42:31.608
because I am a chemist
by training, but I also have

42:31.609 --> 42:33.218
- a psych degree.
- Oh.

42:33.219 --> 42:35.002
Okay. Wow. Great.

42:35.003 --> 42:36.613
A degree from a university?

42:36.614 --> 42:38.310
From a credentialist scam
for laundering privilege?

42:38.311 --> 42:39.398
Amazing.

42:39.399 --> 42:41.052
Well, yeah, I do have a degree.

42:41.053 --> 42:43.794
And I also have read
a lot about this.

42:43.795 --> 42:47.275
You can't talk your way
out of this again.

42:47.276 --> 42:49.539
I'm not a kid anymore.

42:52.760 --> 42:56.415
I think you're in
a kind of echo chamber.

42:56.416 --> 42:58.548
- Echo chamber? Right now?
- Mm-hmm.

42:58.549 --> 43:00.246
Echo?

43:01.900 --> 43:05.250
Yeah, I read the same 5,000
think pieces about that, too.

43:05.251 --> 43:08.427
You're consuming content
on the Internet

43:08.428 --> 43:12.344
that is reinforcing
this sort of warped,

43:12.345 --> 43:14.346
subjective idea of reality.

43:14.347 --> 43:16.653
This is your best shot at me?

43:16.654 --> 43:19.612
Some "rabbit holes" bullshit
you read in The Times?

43:19.613 --> 43:21.266
Come on. Come on.

43:21.267 --> 43:23.224
Can we have a dialogue, please?

43:23.225 --> 43:24.878
Don't call it a dialogue.

43:24.879 --> 43:26.489
This isn't Death of a Salesman.

43:26.490 --> 43:28.360
Okay, can we talk, please?

43:28.361 --> 43:30.014
Or are-are you just gonna
keep doing this?

43:30.015 --> 43:31.581
- We don't need to talk.
- Yes, okay.

43:31.582 --> 43:33.626
Because I know exactly
what you're going to say.

43:33.627 --> 43:36.063
You're going to say
that I'm in some kind of

43:36.064 --> 43:39.850
Internet-induced autohypnotic
feedback loop,

43:39.851 --> 43:42.113
and-and gatekeepers,
and-and norms,

43:42.114 --> 43:44.507
and all that weak
hegemonic horseshit.

43:44.508 --> 43:47.118
But that is precisely
the limp-dick rhetoric

43:47.119 --> 43:48.511
that you've been instructed

43:48.512 --> 43:50.425
to counter the human
insurgency with.

43:50.426 --> 43:53.298
That's the fucking
hyper-normalized dialectic

43:53.299 --> 43:55.735
by which you've convinced
seven and a half billion people

43:55.736 --> 43:57.563
that they're not your captives.

43:57.564 --> 44:02.263
To keep us believing in these
fucking false institutional,

44:02.264 --> 44:05.528
fucking "shy-boleths."

44:05.529 --> 44:07.355
You mean shibboleths.

44:07.356 --> 44:09.009
That's what I said.

44:09.010 --> 44:10.794
- You said...
- Yeah, whatever.

44:10.795 --> 44:12.578
Sorry.

44:12.579 --> 44:15.015
I guess grammar is a false
Andromedan construct as well.

44:15.016 --> 44:16.975
Hmm?

44:22.937 --> 44:24.591
Fucking...

44:34.079 --> 44:35.559
I'm sorry.

44:37.125 --> 44:38.561
You're angry.

44:38.562 --> 44:40.780
I see that.

44:40.781 --> 44:43.000
I-I even think you have
a right to be angry.

44:43.001 --> 44:44.305
- You do?
- Yes.

44:44.306 --> 44:47.352
But we need to have
an honest talk

44:47.353 --> 44:50.616
in good faith about
what is going on here.

44:50.617 --> 44:52.705
Yes, you're right.
Let's-let's-let's talk it out.

44:52.706 --> 44:53.967
Let's create a safe space,

44:53.968 --> 44:56.709
safe words, good faith, dialogue.

44:56.710 --> 44:59.103
We need to talk about this,
we need to talk about that,

44:59.104 --> 45:01.018
and what we talk about
when we talk about

45:01.019 --> 45:02.672
fucking talk, talk, talk, talk,

45:02.673 --> 45:03.977
talk, talk, talk, talk,
talking forever

45:03.978 --> 45:06.197
until we're all fucking dead.

45:06.198 --> 45:07.546
Yeah, I agree.

45:07.547 --> 45:10.549
So, what is this exactly
that you want?

45:10.550 --> 45:11.898
Like, what do you really want?

45:11.899 --> 45:13.335
Is it money?

45:14.685 --> 45:16.773
Your capital has no value to us.

45:16.774 --> 45:19.384
So, what is it then,
a power thing?

45:19.385 --> 45:20.908
A sex thing?

45:23.302 --> 45:25.695
We have no interest
in you sexually.

45:25.696 --> 45:30.482
Irrespective of the fact that
your reproductive organs

45:30.483 --> 45:32.136
may not be compatible with ours,

45:32.137 --> 45:34.705
my cousin and I have also
been chemically castrated.

45:36.576 --> 45:38.664
Oh, Jesus Christ. Okay.

45:38.665 --> 45:41.188
But I figured you might
try to lure us in that way,

45:41.189 --> 45:43.191
hence the precaution.
See, Don?

45:48.414 --> 45:49.719
Don.

45:49.720 --> 45:51.069
Teddy.

45:52.070 --> 45:53.505
Come on.

45:53.506 --> 45:55.289
We have options here.

45:55.290 --> 45:56.726
-No.
- We do.

45:56.727 --> 45:57.988
There are no options.

45:57.989 --> 46:00.294
There are no rules.

46:00.295 --> 46:02.166
There are no deals.

46:02.167 --> 46:03.602
There's no payoff.

46:03.603 --> 46:05.169
There's no money.

46:05.170 --> 46:07.867
There is no legal system.

46:07.868 --> 46:09.303
There's no Congress.

46:09.304 --> 46:11.088
There is no America.

46:11.089 --> 46:14.787
There's no global
democratic order, okay?

46:14.788 --> 46:16.659
So don't talk to me
like I'm a dipshit,

46:16.660 --> 46:18.661
because I'm not a dipshit.

46:18.662 --> 46:20.532
I'm a guy that knows
what the fuck is happening,

46:20.533 --> 46:24.537
and you will not defeat me,
you sick Andromedan fuck!

46:27.192 --> 46:28.976
Teddy, I'm sorry.

46:30.021 --> 46:31.675
You need help.

46:32.937 --> 46:34.939
You're mentally ill.

46:44.818 --> 46:48.125
Everybody denies it at first...

46:48.126 --> 46:50.083
and then they confess.

47:07.798 --> 47:10.364
Fucking...

47:10.365 --> 47:14.194
Fucking fuck! Fucking lie!

47:14.195 --> 47:15.718
Fuck!

47:19.157 --> 47:20.940
Fuck!

48:06.857 --> 48:09.946
I didn't
discover them on my own.

48:09.947 --> 48:12.513
I stand on the shoulders
of giants.

48:12.514 --> 48:15.125
The PA-99-N2 microlensing event

48:15.126 --> 48:17.736
proved that there was
an exoplanet.

48:17.737 --> 48:21.392
And Gideon55's YouTube studies
into Andromedan infiltration

48:21.393 --> 48:23.873
paved the way
for my own research.

48:23.874 --> 48:26.223
But I was the one
who discovered

48:26.224 --> 48:28.312
how to identify them, okay?

48:28.313 --> 48:30.444
I created that content.

48:30.445 --> 48:32.533
Obviously, I've never been
on the ship before,

48:32.534 --> 48:36.015
but I know enough
to render it on my laptop.

48:36.016 --> 48:39.453
The journey there
will be instantaneous.

48:39.454 --> 48:41.455
But once we're on board,

48:41.456 --> 48:43.109
inside their chemical
atmosphere,

48:43.110 --> 48:44.807
they may be able
to hear our thoughts,

48:44.808 --> 48:48.071
so keep your mind clear
and decisive

48:48.072 --> 48:51.030
during the negotiations.

48:51.031 --> 48:56.993
They will see that we are
men of honor and dignity

48:56.994 --> 49:01.780
and that Earth, with its vast
resources and human ingenuity,

49:01.781 --> 49:04.174
has much that we can offer.

49:04.175 --> 49:09.353
So much more than this fucking
worthless death spiral

49:09.354 --> 49:11.050
into chaos and shit.

49:11.051 --> 49:14.184
And if they won't listen
to reason,

49:14.185 --> 49:16.970
well, I have a plan
for that, too.

49:19.668 --> 49:22.584
What will our lives
be like in space?

49:24.630 --> 49:25.892
In space?

49:26.980 --> 49:29.417
Aren't we going
to live in space?

49:31.376 --> 49:33.812
Well, bud, uh...

49:33.813 --> 49:35.770
we'll only be gone
for a few hours.

49:35.771 --> 49:37.468
We're not leaving Earth
for good.

49:37.469 --> 49:39.905
We're saving it.

49:39.906 --> 49:42.865
So we have to stay here?

49:42.866 --> 49:45.519
Well, yeah. Of course.

49:45.520 --> 49:47.217
But we're saving it,

49:47.218 --> 49:50.220
so it'll be a good place
to live again.

49:50.221 --> 49:53.398
So, everything will be okay.

49:55.356 --> 49:57.923
Yeah. I know.

49:57.924 --> 49:59.664
Sorry.

49:59.665 --> 50:01.972
It's okay, man.

50:07.238 --> 50:10.197
Ever since those shots
you gave me...

50:11.242 --> 50:13.243
...I've felt weird

50:13.244 --> 50:15.375
and crazy

50:15.376 --> 50:18.639
and sometimes sad.

50:18.640 --> 50:20.816
Have you felt that way, too?

50:21.817 --> 50:23.906
It'll pass. Don't worry.

50:23.907 --> 50:25.560
Ah.

50:27.388 --> 50:28.650
It'll pass.

51:26.317 --> 51:27.839
Good morning.

51:27.840 --> 51:29.754
You're out of breath.

51:29.755 --> 51:31.408
Oh, yes.

51:31.409 --> 51:33.018
You, um...

51:33.019 --> 51:34.978
you make me nervous.

51:38.416 --> 51:42.549
Um, so, I've-I've been
doing a lot of pondering,

51:42.550 --> 51:46.163
and I think
we should start over.

51:47.555 --> 51:49.122
I want to help you.

51:50.167 --> 51:52.385
And given that,

51:52.386 --> 51:55.432
there is something that I
should have said to you earlier

51:55.433 --> 51:59.175
that I am finally prepared
to say to you now

51:59.176 --> 52:01.308
with conviction.

52:02.831 --> 52:04.659
I am an alien.

52:08.533 --> 52:09.925
I admit it.

52:10.926 --> 52:12.405
You were right all along.

52:12.406 --> 52:15.017
I am an alien.

52:15.018 --> 52:17.323
I mean, you can't blame me
for trying to conceal it

52:17.324 --> 52:19.238
for as long as I did. I...

52:19.239 --> 52:20.631
Part of my mission here on Earth

52:20.632 --> 52:23.200
is to blend in
and so forth, so...

52:26.116 --> 52:27.899
Look, I'm very tired.

52:27.900 --> 52:30.815
And I know that this doesn't...

52:30.816 --> 52:33.426
sound as forceful

52:33.427 --> 52:35.820
or the verisimilitude is not

52:35.821 --> 52:37.735
what you would want it to be,
necessarily,

52:37.736 --> 52:41.086
but I can assure you
I mean what I say.

52:41.087 --> 52:44.525
And I would like to move
forward now to a solution.

52:48.399 --> 52:50.096
I'm an alien.

53:10.421 --> 53:12.292
You want to start over?

53:13.598 --> 53:15.990
Yes.

53:15.991 --> 53:17.601
Good.

53:17.602 --> 53:19.778
Let's start over.

53:22.346 --> 53:25.348
I was hoping
we could agree on your genus

53:25.349 --> 53:28.090
and avoid a painful test,
but you forced my hand.

53:28.091 --> 53:29.874
I-I admitted it.

53:29.875 --> 53:31.528
Okay?

53:31.529 --> 53:33.921
- I admitted it.
- I'm sorry.

53:33.922 --> 53:37.187
I'm a humane person.
I-I do not want to do this.

53:38.536 --> 53:40.624
I'm an alien.

53:40.625 --> 53:42.539
I am an alien!

53:42.540 --> 53:44.323
- I am...
- I agree.

53:44.324 --> 53:46.369
♪ Do you have the time ♪

53:46.370 --> 53:49.459
♪ To listen to me whine ♪

53:49.460 --> 53:54.508
♪ About nothing and everything
all at once? ♪

53:56.075 --> 53:57.467
♪ I am one of those... ♪

53:57.468 --> 54:00.165
Uh, are you sure it works?

54:00.166 --> 54:02.515
She already admitted it.

54:02.516 --> 54:04.517
It killed our family, cuzzie.

54:04.518 --> 54:06.171
Yeah, but...

54:06.172 --> 54:08.086
this doesn't seem right.

54:08.087 --> 54:11.395
♪ Sometimes I give myself
the creeps... ♪

54:12.526 --> 54:14.745
Please stop. Please, please.

54:14.746 --> 54:16.790
Don't. Don't.

54:16.791 --> 54:18.270
Don't, don't, don't do this.
Don't do this.

54:18.271 --> 54:21.186
♪ It all keeps adding up,
I think... ♪

54:21.187 --> 54:22.970
Okay, here comes the first wave.

54:22.971 --> 54:25.234
No, no, no, no, no.
No, no, no, no, no.

54:25.235 --> 54:27.975
No, no, no...

54:33.156 --> 54:34.591
Please don't.

54:34.592 --> 54:36.897
Trust me, Don. Trust me.

54:36.898 --> 54:38.986
Second wave.

54:38.987 --> 54:43.034
♪ She said it's lack of sex
that's bringing me down ♪

54:43.035 --> 54:46.168
♪ I went to a whore ♪

54:46.169 --> 54:48.518
♪ He said my life's a bore ♪

54:48.519 --> 54:50.737
♪ So quit
my whining 'cause... ♪

54:55.003 --> 54:58.571
♪ Sometimes
I give myself the creeps... ♪

54:58.572 --> 55:00.792
Teddy, no!

55:12.847 --> 55:14.892
You'll kill her, Teddy!

55:17.025 --> 55:18.548
Can you stop?

55:18.549 --> 55:20.158
Teddy, stop!

55:20.159 --> 55:21.899
Donny, back up!

55:21.900 --> 55:24.554
Sorry.

55:24.555 --> 55:28.688
♪ Grasping to control ♪

55:28.689 --> 55:30.821
♪ So I better hold on... ♪

55:41.746 --> 55:44.269
What the fuck?

55:44.270 --> 55:46.358
That's enough!

55:48.274 --> 55:50.798
What's wrong with you, man?

55:52.017 --> 55:53.713
She could've died.

55:53.714 --> 55:56.803
No. No, Don,
you don't understand.

55:56.804 --> 55:59.284
What?

55:59.285 --> 56:00.981
It was off the charts.

56:00.982 --> 56:03.375
The output, it's never reached
that threshold before.

56:03.376 --> 56:05.072
"Before"?!

56:05.073 --> 56:07.162
Could you get me
a towel, please?

56:27.748 --> 56:30.446
I wish to...

56:30.447 --> 56:32.927
apologize profusely.

56:35.974 --> 56:38.585
I did not realize...

56:39.630 --> 56:41.152
...Your Majesty.

56:41.153 --> 56:43.067
- What?
- I stupidly thought

56:43.068 --> 56:44.983
you were admin.

56:46.419 --> 56:50.510
I did not realize,
at that voltage...

56:51.685 --> 56:54.426
...you have the royal
genetic code.

56:54.427 --> 56:56.515
I'm sorry.

56:56.516 --> 56:57.865
I didn't know.

56:58.953 --> 57:00.564
I didn't know.

57:05.264 --> 57:07.744
The most important thing I want
to stress to you right now

57:07.745 --> 57:10.007
is I never want
to put this behind us.

57:10.008 --> 57:11.139
Never.

57:12.271 --> 57:14.664
What happened is part
of all of us now.

57:14.665 --> 57:16.013
And it doesn't go away,

57:16.014 --> 57:17.797
and it doesn't get swept
under the rug,

57:17.798 --> 57:19.190
and it doesn't get excused.

57:19.191 --> 57:20.844
Not on my watch.

57:20.845 --> 57:22.803
This one sticks. Forever.

57:23.456 --> 57:25.414
I am putting this up

57:25.415 --> 57:27.633
on the corporate masthead
for all to see.

57:27.634 --> 57:31.943
For everyone in our company
and our industry to learn from.

57:32.900 --> 57:34.292
That's why I'm meeting

57:34.293 --> 57:35.641
all of the victims' families
this week.

57:35.642 --> 57:38.209
To let them know
we are going to do better.

57:38.210 --> 57:39.558
Maybe we don't even
try to market

57:39.559 --> 57:41.343
a product like this anymore.

57:41.344 --> 57:44.998
Or maybe, maybe we take
this experience to grow

57:44.999 --> 57:46.783
and to get this formula right.

57:46.784 --> 57:49.916
Because I really do think,
if done correctly and safely,

57:49.917 --> 57:52.484
this could be a product
that could help someone

57:52.485 --> 57:54.051
like your mom.

57:54.052 --> 57:56.749
But right now, we would like
to do what's right

57:56.750 --> 57:59.012
and cover the expenses
for your mother's treatment

57:59.013 --> 58:02.233
in hopes that her condition
might one day improve.

58:02.234 --> 58:05.105
We will not tolerate the idea
of you or your family

58:05.106 --> 58:06.933
bearing the financial burden
of this.

58:06.934 --> 58:09.283
We are covering all of it.

58:09.284 --> 58:11.024
This one's on us.

58:11.025 --> 58:13.376
And, again, we're just so sorry.

59:01.902 --> 59:03.294
You'll have to excuse me.

59:03.295 --> 59:07.298
It's my best attempt
to approximate

59:07.299 --> 59:10.736
the royal treatment
to which you are accustomed.

59:10.737 --> 59:13.478
Oh, it's great. Thank you.

59:13.479 --> 59:15.828
There was a wig
in the bathroom.

59:15.829 --> 59:17.221
Did you want me to wear that?

59:17.222 --> 59:18.614
No, no. It's just an option.

59:18.615 --> 59:19.832
I'm fine.

59:19.833 --> 59:21.617
And I want to apologize

59:21.618 --> 59:24.750
for not approaching you
with proper courtesy.

59:24.751 --> 59:27.187
Not realizing, of course,
what you were.

59:27.188 --> 59:30.060
That you shared blood
with the emperor himself.

59:30.061 --> 59:32.279
Oh, that's
perfectly all right.

59:32.280 --> 59:35.761
The truth is, we will
never make progress here

59:35.762 --> 59:38.764
if we can't speak
eyeball to eyeball

59:38.765 --> 59:41.463
as the most evolved examples
of our respective species.

59:41.464 --> 59:43.116
I agree.

59:43.117 --> 59:44.510
-Good.
-Excellent.

59:48.471 --> 59:52.126
Well, on that note, enjoy.

01:00:01.701 --> 01:00:03.094
It's a lovely home.

01:00:04.835 --> 01:00:06.226
Thank you.

01:00:06.227 --> 01:00:08.185
Mmm.

01:00:08.186 --> 01:00:09.578
Just you here?

01:00:09.579 --> 01:00:11.667
Yes.

01:00:11.668 --> 01:00:13.321
Always?

01:00:14.584 --> 01:00:15.714
Sorry?

01:00:15.715 --> 01:00:18.108
Has-has it always just been you?

01:00:18.109 --> 01:00:20.719
Um, well...

01:00:20.720 --> 01:00:24.810
I'd prefer if we didn't delve
too deeply into the personal,

01:00:24.811 --> 01:00:26.246
if you don't mind.

01:00:26.247 --> 01:00:27.639
Mmm.

01:00:27.640 --> 01:00:29.336
Sure, that's fine.

01:00:29.337 --> 01:00:30.904
Thank you.

01:00:34.517 --> 01:00:36.169
So, what...

01:00:36.170 --> 01:00:39.085
Why don't you tell me more
about your movement?

01:00:39.086 --> 01:00:40.739
My what?

01:00:40.740 --> 01:00:42.829
Your movement.
What you're doing.

01:00:45.005 --> 01:00:49.008
Respectfully,
we are not a movement.

01:00:49.009 --> 01:00:50.488
Oh.

01:00:50.489 --> 01:00:53.143
A movement is made up
of many people.

01:00:53.144 --> 01:00:54.885
I did this all on my own.

01:00:55.929 --> 01:00:57.321
Of course.

01:00:57.322 --> 01:01:00.019
With the help of my colleague,
of course.

01:01:00.020 --> 01:01:01.325
Well, it's very impressive.

01:01:01.326 --> 01:01:02.587
-Thank you.
-I'm...

01:01:02.588 --> 01:01:06.199
I'm all for people
who can do that.

01:01:06.200 --> 01:01:09.682
You know, the activism thing.

01:01:11.641 --> 01:01:14.599
99.9% of what's called activism

01:01:14.600 --> 01:01:17.123
is really personal exhibitionism

01:01:17.124 --> 01:01:20.518
and brand maintenance
in disguise.

01:01:20.519 --> 01:01:22.564
Mmm. Okay.

01:01:22.565 --> 01:01:24.567
I used to be the same way.

01:01:26.177 --> 01:01:30.354
I ran through the whole
digestive tract in...

01:01:30.355 --> 01:01:32.356
five years?

01:01:32.357 --> 01:01:36.969
Alt-right, alt-lite,
leftist, Marxist.

01:01:36.970 --> 01:01:39.493
All those stupid badges.

01:01:39.494 --> 01:01:42.758
I went shopping hungry, and I
just bought the whole store.

01:01:44.064 --> 01:01:46.283
Mmm.

01:01:46.284 --> 01:01:48.938
But I was just looking
in the wrong places.

01:01:48.939 --> 01:01:52.724
Until I discovered you.

01:01:52.725 --> 01:01:55.379
Well, again,
it is very impressive.

01:01:55.380 --> 01:01:57.730
Thank you.

01:01:59.123 --> 01:02:01.124
You as well, Don.

01:02:01.125 --> 01:02:03.126
- Um...
-You'll...

01:02:03.127 --> 01:02:04.606
You'll have to excuse
my colleague.

01:02:04.607 --> 01:02:06.477
He prefers not to converse.

01:02:06.478 --> 01:02:09.045
Uh, can I go to the bathroom?

01:02:09.046 --> 01:02:11.351
In just a minute, Don.

01:02:11.352 --> 01:02:13.224
We're eating right now.

01:02:18.011 --> 01:02:20.056
I see you're apiarists.

01:02:20.057 --> 01:02:21.579
Of sorts.

01:02:21.580 --> 01:02:23.015
I've taken an interest as well.

01:02:23.016 --> 01:02:25.148
Hmm. So I've heard.

01:02:25.149 --> 01:02:27.324
Magnificent
creatures, honeybees.

01:02:27.325 --> 01:02:28.760
Very much so.

01:02:28.761 --> 01:02:31.763
Earth's most admirable creation.

01:02:31.764 --> 01:02:35.289
Well, shit, I've literally said
those exact words before.

01:02:40.512 --> 01:02:44.559
Right, so, um, what is it
that you admire about them?

01:02:46.823 --> 01:02:48.955
About bees? Uh...

01:02:50.304 --> 01:02:51.827
Complex society.

01:02:51.828 --> 01:02:53.393
Work ethic.

01:02:53.394 --> 01:02:55.091
They do their duty,
they build their worlds

01:02:55.092 --> 01:02:59.662
without complaint or piety
or self-obsession.

01:03:02.316 --> 01:03:03.577
Mm-hmm.

01:03:03.578 --> 01:03:05.015
All true.

01:03:07.887 --> 01:03:12.848
Which is why they're so easy
to exploit, right?

01:03:12.849 --> 01:03:15.720
I just admire their resolve.
That's all.

01:03:15.721 --> 01:03:17.680
Even in the face of peril.

01:03:18.637 --> 01:03:20.465
Well, we can agree on that.

01:03:25.949 --> 01:03:28.037
What sort of peril, by the way?

01:03:28.038 --> 01:03:29.429
Sorry?

01:03:29.430 --> 01:03:31.954
You said bees have faced peril.

01:03:31.955 --> 01:03:33.521
Such as?

01:03:34.827 --> 01:03:36.480
Uh, what do you want me to say?

01:03:36.481 --> 01:03:39.135
Well, just say it.

01:03:39.136 --> 01:03:41.485
- Why don't you say it?
- Nah, you should just say it.

01:03:41.486 --> 01:03:43.052
You go ahead.

01:03:43.053 --> 01:03:44.444
No, I insist.

01:03:44.445 --> 01:03:47.318
No, please. After you.

01:03:48.667 --> 01:03:51.975
Colony collapse disorder.

01:03:57.763 --> 01:04:00.199
Sure, Teddy. Like CCD.

01:04:00.200 --> 01:04:02.506
You're a bit of an expert
on CCD.

01:04:02.507 --> 01:04:05.204
Well, I... I wouldn't
say that exactly.

01:04:05.205 --> 01:04:07.860
Well, I would say that exactly.

01:04:09.035 --> 01:04:11.428
It's all right.
We're just talking.

01:04:11.429 --> 01:04:14.736
So, I take it you're referring
to the neonicotinoids

01:04:14.737 --> 01:04:17.042
that my company makes.

01:04:17.043 --> 01:04:18.957
You know what? Let's just...
let's just leave it.

01:04:18.958 --> 01:04:21.481
No, I-I appreciate your concern.

01:04:21.482 --> 01:04:25.311
I just think your research
is a bit out of date, Teddy.

01:04:25.312 --> 01:04:28.010
Uh, CCD has declined
significantly in recent years.

01:04:28.011 --> 01:04:30.142
The bees are coming back.

01:04:30.143 --> 01:04:32.101
And there's no consensus

01:04:32.102 --> 01:04:36.279
that pesticides were ever
a real threat to begin with.

01:04:36.280 --> 01:04:40.544
Yes, I'm well aware of what
you've all been telling us.

01:04:40.545 --> 01:04:42.764
Thank you.

01:04:42.765 --> 01:04:48.073
I know you want there
to be a master plan, Teddy.

01:04:48.074 --> 01:04:52.512
You want the bees to be dying
so that it can be my fault

01:04:52.513 --> 01:04:54.645
and you don't have to think
about the real reasons

01:04:54.646 --> 01:04:56.039
why species die.

01:04:57.170 --> 01:05:00.651
Immunodeficiencies,
changing habitats,

01:05:00.652 --> 01:05:03.262
genetic factors.

01:05:03.263 --> 01:05:06.048
Or sometimes a species
just winds down.

01:05:07.311 --> 01:05:09.051
"Winds down"?

01:05:09.052 --> 01:05:11.880
Maybe something clicks
in their heads

01:05:11.881 --> 01:05:15.232
and they just know
or they intuit.

01:05:16.407 --> 01:05:19.932
The futility of
the entire enterprise.

01:05:20.977 --> 01:05:23.195
Who knows, right?

01:05:23.196 --> 01:05:25.154
Right. Who knows?

01:05:25.155 --> 01:05:28.287
-That's right.
- So hard to say.

01:05:29.376 --> 01:05:30.813
Who knows, Don?

01:05:34.947 --> 01:05:37.122
We were having a nice dinner.

01:05:37.123 --> 01:05:38.384
We were.

01:05:38.385 --> 01:05:41.911
Nice, quiet, respectful.

01:05:42.912 --> 01:05:44.869
But now we're not.

01:05:44.870 --> 01:05:46.088
No, we're not.

01:05:46.089 --> 01:05:48.700
And why do suppose that is?

01:05:50.397 --> 01:05:52.007
You tell me.

01:05:52.008 --> 01:05:53.791
Because you're lying to me.

01:05:53.792 --> 01:05:55.401
Are you sure
I can't use the bathr...

01:05:55.402 --> 01:05:57.447
Shh!

01:05:57.448 --> 01:05:59.537
Your usual conclusion.

01:06:00.625 --> 01:06:03.235
You're murdering the bees.

01:06:03.236 --> 01:06:04.367
I am not.

01:06:04.368 --> 01:06:07.022
And now you're lying again.

01:06:07.023 --> 01:06:08.371
- Lies.
- Lies.

01:06:08.372 --> 01:06:10.764
- Truth.
- Lies.

01:06:10.765 --> 01:06:13.115
What's the difference?

01:06:13.116 --> 01:06:14.507
I can't change your mind.

01:06:14.508 --> 01:06:16.466
You're right, you can't.

01:06:16.467 --> 01:06:19.382
Because I know who you are.

01:06:19.383 --> 01:06:21.254
I know what you are.

01:06:22.821 --> 01:06:25.606
I know you, too, Teddy.

01:06:27.043 --> 01:06:29.131
Bullshit you do.

01:06:29.132 --> 01:06:31.437
I do.

01:06:31.438 --> 01:06:32.961
You know how I know?

01:06:32.962 --> 01:06:34.485
Fuck you.

01:06:36.400 --> 01:06:38.532
Sandy Gatz.

01:06:41.318 --> 01:06:43.407
What did you say?

01:06:45.061 --> 01:06:46.932
I remember, Teddy.

01:06:48.368 --> 01:06:50.849
That was your mother. Right?

01:06:52.546 --> 01:06:54.112
She is my mother.

01:06:54.113 --> 01:06:55.722
Right, yes. Of course.

01:06:55.723 --> 01:06:57.986
I'm sorry.

01:06:57.987 --> 01:07:00.553
And you will never
say her name again.

01:07:00.554 --> 01:07:01.946
Understand?

01:07:01.947 --> 01:07:03.601
That's fair enough.

01:07:04.732 --> 01:07:06.951
But I do think
we need to discuss...

01:07:06.952 --> 01:07:08.344
W-We actually do not

01:07:08.345 --> 01:07:10.607
because this is not about that.

01:07:10.608 --> 01:07:12.565
With all due respect, Teddy,

01:07:12.566 --> 01:07:14.872
how could this
not be about that?

01:07:14.873 --> 01:07:16.918
We believed
we were helping, Teddy.

01:07:16.919 --> 01:07:18.571
Don't you dare.

01:07:18.572 --> 01:07:21.270
Opioid withdrawal
medication like that

01:07:21.271 --> 01:07:23.011
could've helped your mother

01:07:23.012 --> 01:07:25.361
- and millions like her.
- Stop. Just stop.

01:07:25.362 --> 01:07:28.712
And the clinical trial pay,
that was helping her, too.

01:07:28.713 --> 01:07:31.149
I know it wasn't
a king's ransom, but it...

01:07:31.150 --> 01:07:32.934
Stop right now.

01:07:32.935 --> 01:07:35.980
Obviously, we did not foresee
the complications

01:07:35.981 --> 01:07:37.939
for Sandy or for the others.

01:07:37.940 --> 01:07:39.114
Do not say her name.

01:07:39.115 --> 01:07:40.854
You do not say her name.

01:07:40.855 --> 01:07:43.640
We believed we paid your family
a proper reparation,

01:07:43.641 --> 01:07:45.947
but now I see
it wasn't nearly enough.

01:07:45.948 --> 01:07:47.470
- Stop!
- Not by half,

01:07:47.471 --> 01:07:48.732
not by a fraction.

01:07:48.733 --> 01:07:50.125
- Stop!
- Teddy...

01:07:50.126 --> 01:07:52.083
you're right to distrust me,
you are.

01:07:52.084 --> 01:07:54.477
- I lost myself somewhere, okay?
- Fuck you.

01:07:54.478 --> 01:07:56.044
- Shut the fuck up.
- I...

01:07:56.045 --> 01:07:58.263
I became a human being

01:07:58.264 --> 01:07:59.743
that I told myself
I would never become.

01:07:59.744 --> 01:08:01.614
- Fuck you!
- I'm not denying that,

01:08:01.615 --> 01:08:03.181
but I can help you, Teddy.

01:08:03.182 --> 01:08:04.835
I can still help you.

01:08:04.836 --> 01:08:06.663
And I can still help
your mother.

01:08:06.664 --> 01:08:08.360
I can help her.

01:08:08.361 --> 01:08:09.622
Truly, I can.

01:08:09.623 --> 01:08:11.798
I-I... I mean,

01:08:11.799 --> 01:08:13.888
can you?

01:08:14.846 --> 01:08:16.282
You needed a mother.

01:08:17.370 --> 01:08:18.631
She was never there for you.

01:08:18.632 --> 01:08:19.893
Fucking die, you fucker!

01:08:25.291 --> 01:08:26.988
Fucking kill you!

01:08:26.989 --> 01:08:28.729
I'll fucking kill you!

01:08:33.212 --> 01:08:34.996
Teddy, stop.

01:08:41.612 --> 01:08:43.135
Teddy, stop.

01:09:39.583 --> 01:09:41.062
Get off him!

01:09:41.063 --> 01:09:42.715
You can't beat me,
because you are a loser

01:09:42.716 --> 01:09:44.239
and I am a winner.

01:09:44.240 --> 01:09:45.806
And that's fucking life.

01:10:53.135 --> 01:10:54.483
- Hey.
- Hey.

01:10:54.484 --> 01:10:55.919
How annoying is this, right?

01:10:55.920 --> 01:10:57.442
- No, what's up?
- Mmm.

01:10:57.443 --> 01:10:58.922
No, come on, dude. I know.

01:10:58.923 --> 01:11:00.315
It's like,
"Why'd I even tell this guy

01:11:00.316 --> 01:11:02.055
he could stop by," right?

01:11:02.056 --> 01:11:03.579
It's fine, Casey. What's up?

01:11:03.580 --> 01:11:05.363
Um, sorry.

01:11:05.364 --> 01:11:07.539
I-I actually do have a real
reason to be here, though.

01:11:07.540 --> 01:11:09.106
Uh-huh.

01:11:09.107 --> 01:11:11.239
Um, well, you know how
we're all working

01:11:11.240 --> 01:11:13.024
this missing persons thing?

01:11:14.591 --> 01:11:16.244
Uh, yeah,

01:11:16.245 --> 01:11:18.421
I just had a couple questions
to run by you, actually.

01:11:19.378 --> 01:11:20.552
Don't worry.

01:11:20.553 --> 01:11:22.641
Obviously, I just, um...

01:11:22.642 --> 01:11:25.384
Sorry, could I actually
come in, maybe?

01:11:26.429 --> 01:11:27.777
Uh, yeah. No, sure.

01:11:27.778 --> 01:11:29.387
Come on in.

01:11:29.388 --> 01:11:31.042
Dude, thank you.
I really appreciate that.

01:11:38.180 --> 01:11:39.702
We are not alone.

01:11:39.703 --> 01:11:41.225
Huh?

01:11:41.226 --> 01:11:43.532
Nothing. Just, you know,

01:11:43.533 --> 01:11:45.186
"We are not alone."

01:11:45.187 --> 01:11:46.535
Oh, right.

01:11:46.536 --> 01:11:48.189
Well, we're not.

01:11:48.190 --> 01:11:49.581
- Uh...
-Right.

01:11:49.582 --> 01:11:51.540
You want some water or...

01:11:51.541 --> 01:11:54.020
That'd be great. Thank you.

01:11:55.414 --> 01:11:57.589
Gotta tell you, man, it's, uh,

01:11:57.590 --> 01:11:59.679
pretty weird being back in here.

01:12:00.854 --> 01:12:02.639
A lot of feelings.

01:12:07.078 --> 01:12:09.601
Yeah, well, same old shit.

01:12:09.602 --> 01:12:10.994
Hmm.

01:12:10.995 --> 01:12:12.909
Thank you.

01:12:12.910 --> 01:12:15.607
Scared the, uh,
chair's gonna run away?

01:12:15.608 --> 01:12:17.219
What?

01:12:19.873 --> 01:12:22.484
Oh. No.

01:12:22.485 --> 01:12:25.617
My mom, she used to have
fits or whatever,

01:12:25.618 --> 01:12:27.533
so we'd-we'd nail
the chair down.

01:12:28.926 --> 01:12:30.232
Yeah.

01:12:32.103 --> 01:12:33.625
Uh-oh.

01:12:33.626 --> 01:12:35.497
What?

01:12:35.498 --> 01:12:37.369
My archnemesis.

01:12:39.284 --> 01:12:41.154
Ah.

01:12:41.155 --> 01:12:43.461
You want a piece of cake?

01:12:43.462 --> 01:12:45.637
I mean, if you insist.

01:12:47.292 --> 01:12:50.076
Yeah, I love this stuff.

01:12:56.127 --> 01:12:58.433
So, um, you had
some questions or...?

01:12:58.434 --> 01:13:00.696
Oh. Uh, yeah, sorry.

01:13:00.697 --> 01:13:02.524
Um, you're still
at Auxolith, right?

01:13:02.525 --> 01:13:04.047
Yeah.

01:13:04.048 --> 01:13:06.658
So you must know all about
the Fuller case?

01:13:06.659 --> 01:13:09.270
I mean, I heard a little, yeah.

01:13:09.271 --> 01:13:10.793
On the news?

01:13:10.794 --> 01:13:12.969
I don't get the news
from the news.

01:13:12.970 --> 01:13:14.666
Right. Um, of course. Sorry.

01:13:14.667 --> 01:13:16.233
I'm just here on a hunch, really.

01:13:16.234 --> 01:13:18.148
See, this missing lady,
her phone

01:13:18.149 --> 01:13:20.324
pinged a cell tower in the area
the night of the abduction.

01:13:20.325 --> 01:13:21.673
Thank you. Thank you very much.

01:13:21.674 --> 01:13:23.284
Oh.

01:13:23.285 --> 01:13:25.808
Well, those things have
a pretty wide radius,

01:13:25.809 --> 01:13:28.201
- though, right?
- Yeah, no, for sure.

01:13:28.202 --> 01:13:31.117
It's just that her car was
also snapped by a speed trap

01:13:31.118 --> 01:13:33.816
near the intersection
down the road over here.

01:13:33.817 --> 01:13:35.166
Oh, yeah?

01:13:36.210 --> 01:13:37.863
I know. I'm, uh...

01:13:37.864 --> 01:13:39.561
You know, long shot, right?

01:13:39.562 --> 01:13:41.911
But, I don't know,
it's a sparsely populated area.

01:13:41.912 --> 01:13:43.782
Figured I'd check in
with the local residents.

01:13:43.783 --> 01:13:47.787
See if, uh, you or Don
seen anything peculiar.

01:13:48.745 --> 01:13:50.223
Uh...

01:13:50.224 --> 01:13:52.269
No, no.

01:13:52.270 --> 01:13:53.792
Well, uh, hmm.

01:13:53.793 --> 01:13:55.707
Let's see here.

01:13:55.708 --> 01:13:59.146
For starters, have you seen...

01:14:00.539 --> 01:14:02.888
...this car?

01:14:02.889 --> 01:14:04.542
Uh-uh.

01:14:04.543 --> 01:14:08.242
What about, uh, this woman?

01:14:09.635 --> 01:14:12.158
I mean, yeah,
she-she owns my work, yeah.

01:14:12.159 --> 01:14:13.725
But I haven't seen her, no.

01:14:13.726 --> 01:14:15.161
You haven't seen her in person?

01:14:15.162 --> 01:14:16.293
No.

01:14:16.294 --> 01:14:19.340
I scan packages, so I wouldn't.

01:14:19.341 --> 01:14:21.211
No, no. Dude, I-I know.
I'm-I'm sorry.

01:14:21.212 --> 01:14:23.126
Um, how about your neighbors?

01:14:23.127 --> 01:14:24.997
They say anything about,
I don't know,

01:14:24.998 --> 01:14:27.826
any out-of-the-ordinary
activity?

01:14:27.827 --> 01:14:30.352
Uh, I mean,
I don't know them, really.

01:14:31.614 --> 01:14:33.310
Right. I-I'm sorry, man.

01:14:33.311 --> 01:14:36.445
Uh, I'm really grasping
at straws here.

01:14:37.837 --> 01:14:39.708
Uh...

01:14:39.709 --> 01:14:43.102
Look, I mainly just wanted
to check up on you, man.

01:14:43.103 --> 01:14:44.887
I know the last thing you want

01:14:44.888 --> 01:14:47.672
is for your fucked-up
babysitter from 20 years ago

01:14:47.673 --> 01:14:52.242
stopping by,
feeling guilty about, um...

01:14:52.243 --> 01:14:55.985
you know, whatever
went down, uh, but...

01:14:55.986 --> 01:14:57.726
Sometimes I pass by this place,

01:14:57.727 --> 01:15:03.122
and I just get this fucking
sad, awful feeling, like,

01:15:03.123 --> 01:15:05.082
"What's going on in there?"

01:15:06.518 --> 01:15:08.127
You know?

01:15:08.128 --> 01:15:09.781
Not much.

01:15:20.967 --> 01:15:22.359
Where is he?

01:15:33.197 --> 01:15:34.284
Don?

01:15:34.285 --> 01:15:36.982
Look at me, Don.

01:15:36.983 --> 01:15:38.549
Put the gun down.

01:15:38.550 --> 01:15:40.029
Look at me.

01:15:40.030 --> 01:15:42.293
I know you would never hurt me.

01:15:56.960 --> 01:15:59.962
Thank you, Don.

01:15:59.963 --> 01:16:04.358
You could've shot me earlier
upstairs, but you didn't.

01:16:07.100 --> 01:16:10.408
How you behaved
was honestly heroic.

01:16:11.931 --> 01:16:14.151
I don't use that word lightly.

01:16:15.457 --> 01:16:17.675
You have been the only thing
stopping him

01:16:17.676 --> 01:16:20.461
from doing God knows what to me.

01:16:20.462 --> 01:16:22.942
I don't talk to you.

01:16:24.030 --> 01:16:26.771
That's how it is.

01:16:26.772 --> 01:16:29.295
So stay quiet.

01:16:29.296 --> 01:16:31.385
But you know
this is crazy, right?

01:16:32.778 --> 01:16:35.127
You know this is wrong.

01:16:35.128 --> 01:16:36.651
I know you know that.

01:16:36.652 --> 01:16:37.869
Shut up.

01:16:37.870 --> 01:16:39.741
I'm just saying.

01:16:39.742 --> 01:16:41.743
There is a world, Don.

01:16:41.744 --> 01:16:44.746
There is a world
where we help you

01:16:44.747 --> 01:16:47.226
and your cousin and your aunt,

01:16:47.227 --> 01:16:51.448
where reparations are paid
and a page is turned.

01:16:51.449 --> 01:16:53.885
All of that can happen for you.

01:16:53.886 --> 01:16:55.931
No. You're...

01:16:55.932 --> 01:16:58.281
You're gonna get
me and Teddy arrested.

01:16:58.282 --> 01:16:59.978
No, I wouldn't.

01:16:59.979 --> 01:17:02.677
And-and if you're right
and Teddy gets arrested,

01:17:02.678 --> 01:17:06.507
it's... it'll all be different
for you, Don.

01:17:06.508 --> 01:17:09.379
It will, if you let me go.

01:17:09.380 --> 01:17:10.554
Stop.

01:17:10.555 --> 01:17:12.514
I know what you're doing.

01:17:14.733 --> 01:17:19.956
All he does is drag you deeper
and deeper into a pit.

01:17:21.348 --> 01:17:24.394
He never actually offers you
a way out for you.

01:17:25.701 --> 01:17:28.877
I can do that for you, Don.

01:17:28.878 --> 01:17:30.574
I want to do that for you.

01:17:30.575 --> 01:17:33.316
I said, shut up!

01:17:33.317 --> 01:17:34.796
It's okay.

01:17:34.797 --> 01:17:37.712
I know you're confused
and frustrated.

01:17:37.713 --> 01:17:41.629
No one in the universe
could possibly blame you.

01:17:41.630 --> 01:17:43.500
Shut up.

01:17:43.501 --> 01:17:45.067
Put the gun down.

01:17:45.068 --> 01:17:46.808
Just talk to me.

01:17:46.809 --> 01:17:48.200
No.

01:17:48.201 --> 01:17:50.115
Sit down and talk to me.
Put the gun down.

01:17:50.116 --> 01:17:54.772
Just shut up, alien filth.

01:17:54.773 --> 01:17:57.167
He ever show up again?

01:18:00.779 --> 01:18:02.824
Fucking asshole.

01:18:02.825 --> 01:18:05.305
Sorry. I know he's your dad
and you probably love him.

01:18:06.480 --> 01:18:08.613
I literally
wouldn't recognize him.

01:18:12.574 --> 01:18:16.141
Look, Teddy, um...

01:18:16.142 --> 01:18:19.537
I know it was a long time ago,
what I did to you, man.

01:18:20.494 --> 01:18:21.582
It's fine.

01:18:21.583 --> 01:18:23.322
No. It wasn't fine.

01:18:23.323 --> 01:18:25.368
It-it was wrong,
but I promise you,

01:18:25.369 --> 01:18:27.109
it's-it's not 'cause I liked it.

01:18:27.110 --> 01:18:28.719
It was just...

01:18:28.720 --> 01:18:29.938
you know, probably
some weird power thing.

01:18:29.939 --> 01:18:33.202
I was... I was young
and lost, and...

01:18:33.203 --> 01:18:37.510
I promise you, dude, I never,
ever did that to anybody else.

01:18:37.511 --> 01:18:39.948
Just forget it. It's done.

01:18:39.949 --> 01:18:41.253
Seriously.

01:18:41.254 --> 01:18:44.126
- Really?
- Mm-hmm.

01:18:48.784 --> 01:18:49.784
Hey, you should read this.

01:18:49.785 --> 01:18:51.917
This shit helped me a lot.

01:18:53.658 --> 01:18:55.225
Thank you, dude.

01:18:56.226 --> 01:18:58.445
Hey, you want to see my bees?

01:19:00.622 --> 01:19:03.101
Someone's up there, right?

01:19:03.102 --> 01:19:05.930
Shut up.

01:19:05.931 --> 01:19:07.628
Is it the police?

01:19:07.629 --> 01:19:09.978
I said, shut up.

01:19:09.979 --> 01:19:11.806
It is.

01:19:11.807 --> 01:19:14.765
And, Don, they're gonna
arrest your cousin.

01:19:14.766 --> 01:19:17.028
But it is not too late for you.

01:19:17.029 --> 01:19:20.162
Please, stop.

01:19:20.163 --> 01:19:22.512
If you let me go right now,

01:19:22.513 --> 01:19:24.688
everything will work out
for you.

01:19:24.689 --> 01:19:25.950
No, it won't.

01:19:25.951 --> 01:19:27.997
It will, Don.

01:19:29.302 --> 01:19:30.694
I promise.

01:19:30.695 --> 01:19:32.261
You don't understand.

01:19:32.262 --> 01:19:34.655
There's nothing left for me.

01:19:34.656 --> 01:19:37.180
Teddy is all I have.

01:19:38.224 --> 01:19:41.357
We'll find something else
for you.

01:19:41.358 --> 01:19:42.706
You don't need him.

01:19:42.707 --> 01:19:44.839
Yes, I do.

01:19:44.840 --> 01:19:46.755
I love him.

01:19:48.147 --> 01:19:50.453
Sorry I couldn't
help you find that lady.

01:19:50.454 --> 01:19:51.672
It's all right, man.

01:19:59.942 --> 01:20:01.203
I got it.

01:20:01.204 --> 01:20:02.639
Thanks.

01:20:02.640 --> 01:20:05.034
- Be gentle.
- Yep, yep.

01:20:11.083 --> 01:20:15.304
There is so much else
out there, Don.

01:20:15.305 --> 01:20:17.262
No, there's not.

01:20:17.263 --> 01:20:18.873
Not here.

01:20:18.874 --> 01:20:20.265
Then where?

01:20:20.266 --> 01:20:23.051
Where do you want to go, Don?

01:20:23.052 --> 01:20:24.530
We can go there.

01:20:24.531 --> 01:20:26.142
I'll take you there.

01:20:27.273 --> 01:20:30.362
If you are an alien,
will you help me?

01:20:30.363 --> 01:20:33.714
Don, that's enough of that.
Please.

01:20:33.715 --> 01:20:35.237
You know I'm not an alien.

01:20:35.238 --> 01:20:36.847
You know that.

01:20:36.848 --> 01:20:41.331
But if you are,
would you take me with you?

01:20:42.724 --> 01:20:44.115
What?

01:20:44.116 --> 01:20:45.943
If all of this is true

01:20:45.944 --> 01:20:49.425
and you have a sh-- spaceship,

01:20:49.426 --> 01:20:52.298
would you take me away
from here?

01:20:55.780 --> 01:20:57.912
Of course, Don.

01:20:57.913 --> 01:20:59.697
Yes, absolutely.

01:21:00.654 --> 01:21:02.439
I'll take you with me.

01:21:03.483 --> 01:21:06.007
We'll leave Earth.

01:21:06.008 --> 01:21:08.967
I promise
that's what'll happen, okay?

01:21:10.186 --> 01:21:11.883
If you let me go.

01:21:15.669 --> 01:21:17.453
Thank you...

01:21:17.454 --> 01:21:19.629
but not without Teddy.

01:21:19.630 --> 01:21:22.197
Please, Don,
we don't have much time.

01:21:22.198 --> 01:21:24.286
Th-They're gonna break in here
at any minute,

01:21:24.287 --> 01:21:26.810
and then I won't be able
to help you.

01:21:29.901 --> 01:21:31.424
Come on.

01:21:44.611 --> 01:21:46.134
Okay.

01:21:46.135 --> 01:21:48.354
I'm ready to leave.

01:21:49.355 --> 01:21:51.095
Okay.

01:21:51.096 --> 01:21:54.925
Can you do one thing for me?

01:21:54.926 --> 01:22:00.671
Tell Teddy that I'm sorry
and that I love him.

01:22:02.586 --> 01:22:04.327
I will.

01:22:11.290 --> 01:22:13.117
The fuck?

01:22:17.731 --> 01:22:20.647
Jesus fucking Christ.

01:22:21.910 --> 01:22:24.259
Fuck.

01:22:52.636 --> 01:22:54.158
Don?

01:22:54.159 --> 01:22:56.074
Don!

01:22:58.163 --> 01:22:59.598
Jesus!

01:22:59.599 --> 01:23:01.035
Don.

01:23:01.036 --> 01:23:02.819
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

01:23:02.820 --> 01:23:04.603
I swear to you,
he did it to himself.

01:23:04.604 --> 01:23:06.040
He thought the police were
coming... -Don. No, no, no.

01:23:06.041 --> 01:23:07.302
...and he panicked,
and he just freaked out.

01:23:07.303 --> 01:23:08.607
Teddy, no. No.

01:23:08.608 --> 01:23:10.174
- What did you say to him?
- Nothing.

01:23:11.873 --> 01:23:15.092
What fucking filth did you
fill his sad brain with,

01:23:15.093 --> 01:23:16.485
you demon from hell?

01:23:16.486 --> 01:23:18.617
He was under
extreme pressure, Teddy.

01:23:18.618 --> 01:23:20.968
- He cracked.
- And you cracked him!

01:23:20.969 --> 01:23:23.361
You poisoned his heart
with lies and bullshit

01:23:23.362 --> 01:23:25.886
until his whole fucking world
collapsed, didn't you?

01:23:25.887 --> 01:23:27.931
You fed him
a fucking fairy tale.

01:23:27.932 --> 01:23:30.020
He did all of this for you,
you fucking maniac.

01:23:30.021 --> 01:23:31.674
Don't kill me, Teddy.

01:23:31.675 --> 01:23:34.721
I have a cure for your mother.

01:23:35.679 --> 01:23:38.028
- What?
- There's a cure.

01:23:38.029 --> 01:23:40.379
You can save her.

01:23:41.467 --> 01:23:42.772
What are you saying?

01:23:42.773 --> 01:23:44.948
Inside of her,

01:23:44.949 --> 01:23:46.907
a big change is taking place.

01:23:46.908 --> 01:23:49.735
It's an entire rearranging

01:23:49.736 --> 01:23:51.912
of her genetic code.

01:23:51.913 --> 01:23:53.826
She was the first sample.

01:23:53.827 --> 01:23:55.524
It's a very important
Andromedan experiment,

01:23:55.525 --> 01:23:57.526
and it takes
four to five years.

01:23:57.527 --> 01:23:59.528
But if it succeeds,
she will wake up.

01:23:59.529 --> 01:24:01.791
Well, what if
it doesn't succeed?

01:24:01.792 --> 01:24:03.488
Then she'll die.

01:24:03.489 --> 01:24:05.838
But if we chemically terminate
the experiment,

01:24:05.839 --> 01:24:07.928
she will wake up,
she'll wake up.

01:24:07.929 --> 01:24:10.626
Well, how...
how-how do we do that?

01:24:10.627 --> 01:24:12.454
- You have my car?
- Yes.

01:24:12.455 --> 01:24:14.543
Okay. So, in my car,

01:24:14.544 --> 01:24:18.286
in the trunk, in the back,
there is a bottle.

01:24:18.287 --> 01:24:21.898
It's a yellow jug, and it says
"monoethylene glycol."

01:24:21.899 --> 01:24:23.552
Antifreeze.
But forget the label.

01:24:23.553 --> 01:24:25.119
It's not antifreeze.
It's the cure.

01:24:25.120 --> 01:24:28.165
I keep it in my car,
in the trunk,

01:24:28.166 --> 01:24:30.994
in the antifreeze jug
to hide it.

01:24:30.995 --> 01:24:32.518
For safety.

01:24:34.956 --> 01:24:36.913
If...

01:24:36.914 --> 01:24:39.568
i-if this experiment
is so important,

01:24:39.569 --> 01:24:42.049
why would you allow me
to cancel it? Huh?

01:24:42.050 --> 01:24:44.094
There are multiple experiments

01:24:44.095 --> 01:24:45.967
happening all over the world--
your mother's one of dozens.

01:24:47.272 --> 01:24:48.490
Just trust me.

01:24:48.491 --> 01:24:49.839
I'm chained up here.

01:24:49.840 --> 01:24:52.102
I have no way of escaping.
Why would I lie?

01:25:00.807 --> 01:25:02.199
-  -
- That's for Don,

01:25:02.200 --> 01:25:03.722
you fucking virus.

01:27:37.921 --> 01:27:40.315
It's not antifreeze, Mom.

01:27:41.490 --> 01:27:43.448
Don't worry.

01:28:23.532 --> 01:28:25.751
Wake up, Mom. Wake up.

01:28:27.927 --> 01:28:30.059
Come on. Come on.

01:28:35.587 --> 01:28:37.022
Please, Mom. Please.

01:28:37.023 --> 01:28:39.155
Come on, come on. Wake up.

01:29:04.921 --> 01:29:06.227
Come on.

01:29:43.525 --> 01:29:44.655
Mom?

01:29:44.656 --> 01:29:45.874
Wake up.

01:29:45.875 --> 01:29:47.919
You can do it.

01:29:47.920 --> 01:29:49.705
Wake up.

01:30:01.238 --> 01:30:03.458
Fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck,
fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck.

01:30:13.859 --> 01:30:15.338
NURSE [in distance]:
201, now!

01:30:32.530 --> 01:30:34.489
Hey! Hey!

01:30:35.533 --> 01:30:36.838
Hey!

01:31:08.784 --> 01:31:11.525
You fucking monster.

01:31:11.526 --> 01:31:14.049
How many were Andromedans?

01:31:14.050 --> 01:31:16.181
You-you... you lied to me.

01:31:16.182 --> 01:31:18.923
How many were Andromedans?!

01:31:20.883 --> 01:31:23.364
- Two.
- Two?

01:31:25.888 --> 01:31:27.584
You miserable fucking idiot.

01:31:27.585 --> 01:31:28.933
Do you know what you've done?

01:31:28.934 --> 01:31:30.370
You...

01:31:30.371 --> 01:31:31.719
you killed her.

01:31:31.720 --> 01:31:33.024
Quiet.

01:31:34.679 --> 01:31:38.813
And I'll tell you why it is
I resemble a human.

01:31:38.814 --> 01:31:41.555
Our 75th emperor
first discovered the Earth.

01:31:43.819 --> 01:31:46.429
This planet was ruled
by dinosaurs,

01:31:46.430 --> 01:31:50.433
magnificent creatures with
a complex but stable ecosystem.

01:31:50.434 --> 01:31:52.957
Oh.

01:31:52.958 --> 01:31:56.919
But we inadvertently spread
a fatal virus to the planet.

01:31:58.268 --> 01:32:00.443
And the emperor was struck
with guilt,

01:32:00.444 --> 01:32:02.533
watching all of Earth's
creatures perish.

01:32:03.665 --> 01:32:05.666
So he gave new life
to this planet.

01:32:05.667 --> 01:32:09.017
Life resembling us.

01:32:09.018 --> 01:32:11.062
The early test humans
could barely stand,

01:32:11.063 --> 01:32:14.589
but soon they walked
and began to reproduce.

01:32:16.112 --> 01:32:19.157
A civilization was born
in harmony with nature.

01:32:19.158 --> 01:32:21.856
Atlantis.

01:32:21.857 --> 01:32:24.424
We were worshipped as gods.

01:32:24.425 --> 01:32:28.079
But some humans wished
to surpass us,

01:32:28.080 --> 01:32:30.821
so they began creating
their own new,

01:32:30.822 --> 01:32:34.999
lab-grown humans
that were stronger.

01:32:35.000 --> 01:32:36.784
But the new humans were
also more aggressive,

01:32:36.785 --> 01:32:39.090
so a conflict broke out

01:32:39.091 --> 01:32:41.658
that eventually resulted in
a thermonuclear war.

01:32:41.659 --> 01:32:44.705
And in the war's wake, all
of humanity was extinguished,

01:32:44.706 --> 01:32:47.795
save for a select few,
who built an ark

01:32:47.796 --> 01:32:50.101
and traveled the oceans
for a century.

01:32:50.102 --> 01:32:52.713
When it was finally safe
to resurface on dry land,

01:32:52.714 --> 01:32:54.802
the leaders of the ark died,

01:32:54.803 --> 01:32:57.979
leaving behind
only a few mutant specimens

01:32:57.980 --> 01:33:01.243
of degraded semi-humans.

01:33:01.244 --> 01:33:02.985
The apes.

01:33:04.073 --> 01:33:06.248
Evolution resumed
but toward chaos.

01:33:06.249 --> 01:33:09.512
The newly evolved human beings,
your current ancestors,

01:33:09.513 --> 01:33:13.385
fought amongst themselves
in an endless cycle of war,

01:33:13.386 --> 01:33:16.345
genocide,
ecological destruction.

01:33:16.346 --> 01:33:18.390
They brutalized Earth.

01:33:18.391 --> 01:33:20.784
They ruined her waters,
ravaged her climate,

01:33:20.785 --> 01:33:23.657
poisoned themselves
with drugs and technology.

01:33:23.658 --> 01:33:26.224
And even when presented
with irrefutable evidence

01:33:26.225 --> 01:33:31.882
of their own self-destruction,
the humans continued unabated.

01:33:31.883 --> 01:33:35.407
Even I myself became more human,

01:33:35.408 --> 01:33:37.105
more selfish and cruel,

01:33:37.106 --> 01:33:40.413
the longer I stayed here
amongst your kind.

01:33:41.589 --> 01:33:44.025
But humans can't help
the way they are.

01:33:44.026 --> 01:33:46.158
It's in your genes.

01:33:47.290 --> 01:33:49.596
The genes implanted
by your ancestors

01:33:49.597 --> 01:33:51.380
to strengthen themselves.

01:33:51.381 --> 01:33:55.036
It gets reproduced in your
bodies, and it grows stronger.

01:33:55.037 --> 01:33:59.475
We Andromedans are here to
eliminate that suicidal gene.

01:33:59.476 --> 01:34:02.043
To save humanity.

01:34:02.044 --> 01:34:05.916
But also to save Earth
from you and your kind.

01:34:05.917 --> 01:34:07.701
No.

01:34:09.442 --> 01:34:12.096
No, you came here to kill us.

01:34:12.097 --> 01:34:13.533
Y-You came to kill us.

01:34:13.534 --> 01:34:15.404
Well, that's wrong.
That's wrong, Teddy.

01:34:15.405 --> 01:34:16.971
Some of us would have preferred

01:34:16.972 --> 01:34:19.016
to simply eliminate
your species,

01:34:19.017 --> 01:34:20.714
but the emperor believed
there was still hope,

01:34:20.715 --> 01:34:24.065
so the experiments.

01:34:24.066 --> 01:34:25.806
The experiments
your mother was a part of.

01:34:25.807 --> 01:34:27.895
She was chosen
because she was weak.

01:34:27.896 --> 01:34:29.549
Because she was broken.

01:34:29.550 --> 01:34:31.638
If we could correct her,

01:34:31.639 --> 01:34:34.554
perhaps all humans
could be corrected.

01:34:34.555 --> 01:34:37.034
But you... you killed her!

01:34:37.035 --> 01:34:38.993
You killed her.

01:34:38.994 --> 01:34:40.560
I figured you'd be apprehended

01:34:40.561 --> 01:34:42.257
feeding antifreeze
to a coma patient

01:34:42.258 --> 01:34:45.042
and then I'd be freed
and could return to my work.

01:34:45.043 --> 01:34:49.003
But you actually got away
with it, you sick ape.

01:34:49.004 --> 01:34:50.439
I'm not a sick ape.

01:34:50.440 --> 01:34:52.268
You are a sick ape.

01:34:53.486 --> 01:34:55.139
Listen, there are other
test subjects

01:34:55.140 --> 01:34:56.706
who are showing progress,

01:34:56.707 --> 01:34:58.490
and we must show the emperor
the truth.

01:34:58.491 --> 01:35:00.623
Tomorrow.

01:35:00.624 --> 01:35:02.277
During the lunar eclipse.

01:35:02.278 --> 01:35:04.975
Why?

01:35:04.976 --> 01:35:06.803
Teddy, listen, I know, I know.

01:35:06.804 --> 01:35:08.718
You may hate me,

01:35:08.719 --> 01:35:11.765
you may want me dead--
I don't blame you--

01:35:11.766 --> 01:35:14.550
but I have the information
you need to save Earth,

01:35:14.551 --> 01:35:16.204
and you know I do.

01:35:16.205 --> 01:35:18.162
You're a fucking demon.

01:35:18.163 --> 01:35:21.209
This is our destiny, Teddy Gatz.

01:35:21.210 --> 01:35:23.211
Yours and mine.

01:35:23.212 --> 01:35:25.736
And the hour is almost upon us.

01:35:27.303 --> 01:35:29.086
Yay.

01:35:40.533 --> 01:35:42.230
Jesus, Ms. Fuller?

01:35:42.231 --> 01:35:43.492
Hi, Ricky.

01:35:43.493 --> 01:35:45.059
How are you? I'm back.

01:35:45.060 --> 01:35:46.582
Could you buzz me in, please?

01:35:46.583 --> 01:35:48.236
Are you okay?
Are you-you all right?

01:35:48.237 --> 01:35:49.498
Oh, I'm all right.

01:35:49.499 --> 01:35:51.108
Everything's been sorted out.

01:35:51.109 --> 01:35:52.633
Could you just...
could you buzz me in, please?

01:35:53.634 --> 01:35:55.505
Thank you, Ricky.

01:36:20.312 --> 01:36:22.924
Park in your usual spot.

01:36:25.840 --> 01:36:27.624
Don't worry, Don.

01:36:28.973 --> 01:36:31.672
You're coming with me.
I'm taking you with me.

01:36:46.077 --> 01:36:47.469
Hi, Tony.

01:36:47.470 --> 01:36:49.733
There you go.
Have a good evening.

01:37:02.224 --> 01:37:03.703
Hello.

01:37:09.405 --> 01:37:11.189
Doors opening.

01:37:16.107 --> 01:37:17.979
Doors closing.

01:37:23.767 --> 01:37:25.246
Hi.

01:37:25.247 --> 01:37:27.074
Good to see you.

01:37:27.075 --> 01:37:28.511
It's good to be back.

01:37:29.512 --> 01:37:31.079
Hmm.

